\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Majors\b0\par\par\uc2 1,840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2011\par 01:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range   Larger Range \par USD/JPY    75.95-77.10      75.00-77.40 \par EUR/USD   1.4331-1.4453    1.4294-1.4518 \par AUD/USD   1.0311-1.0481    1.0242-1.0557 \par NZD/USD   0.8118-0.8288    0.8061-0.8338 \par GBP/USD   1.6442-1.6554    1.6419-1.6618 \par USD/CHF   0.7805-0.7921    0.7767-0.7959 \par USD/CAD   0.9823-0.9925    0.9796-0.9937 \par EUR/JPY   109.73-110.72    109.03-111.05 \par EUR/GBP   0.8682-0.8746    0.8652-0.8808 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent high and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/JPY - to consolidate with risks skewed higher after hitting record low of 75.95 on Friday. Pair underpinned by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  media reports of likely \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BOJ considering further monetary easing in tandem with possible MOF action. However, after vice finance minister for international affairs Nakao told The Wall Street Journal Friday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities don't have plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  often and don't use \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a daily tool, "market confidence in fading any (USD/JPY) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  driven spike is going to remain high," says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . USD/JPY also supported by Japan importer demand. But USD/JPY gains tempered by flows to safe-haven JPY amid elevated investor risk aversion (VIX fear gauge rose 0.89% to 43.05), sharp Wall Street losses Friday (DJIA down 1.57%) on jitters over potential global recession and health of European banking system; Japan exporter sales, negative USD sentiment (ICE spot dollar index last 74.11 vs 74.37 early Friday), lower U.S. Treasury yields, ultra-loose U.S. monetary policy; increased speculation that Fed Chairman Bernanke may signal further monetary stimulus when he speaks at Friday's Jackson Hole economic policy symposium - such as extending maturity of assets that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds. Data focus: 1230 GMT U.S. July Chicago Fed National Activity Index. USD/JPY daily chart mixed as MACD flat, stochastics turning bullish at oversold. Resistance at 77.00-77.10 band (Friday's high-Aug. 15 high); breach would target 77.30-77.40 band (Aug. 11 high-Aug. 10 high), then 77.86 (Aug. 9 high), 78.48 (Aug. 8 high), 79.42 (Aug. 5 high) and 80.25 (Aug. 4 high). Support at 75.95 (Friday's low); breach would expose downside to psychological 75.00 level, then 74.20 (projected base of descending channel formed with April 2009 high of 101.45 and Nov. 2009 low of 84.81 on weekly chart).\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD - to range-trade. Undermined by weak investor risk sentiment, concerns over euro-zone financial system as worries escalated over European banks' access to funding; worries that Europe's latest bailout for Greece is in danger of collapsing over whether countries that have pledged to provide aid should receive cash collateral; perceived inability of EU leaders to solve the region's debt crisis as German Chancellor Merkel on German TV ZDF Sunday repeated her opposition to issuing common euro-zone bonds. But EUR/USD downside limited by negative USD sentiment; sovereign demand for euro; expectations of ECB's bond-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - there were reports Friday that ECB was checking Italian bond prices; EUR demand on buoyant EUR/JPY cross as threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overhangs. EUR/USD daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics bearish near overbought. Support at 1.4331 (hourly chart), then at 1.4294 (hourly chart) and 1.4258 (Friday's low); breach would target 1.4237 (Aug. 15 low), then 1.4185 (uptrend support line from July 12 low of 1.3835), 1.4149 (Aug. 12 low), 1.4103 (Aug. 11 reaction low) and 1.4055 (Aug. 5 reaction low). Resistance at 1.4453 (Friday's high, matching Thursday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.4518 (Wednesday's high), then 1.4537 (July 27 reaction high), 1.4580 (July 4 reaction high) and 1.4696 (June 7 reaction high).\par \par \uc2 AUD/USD - to trade in lower range. Undermined by weak global risk sentiment. But AUD/USD losses tempered by negative USD sentiment, AUD-USD interest rate differential, sovereign demand for Aussie, firmer commodity prices (CRB spot index closed up 3.05 Friday at 329.47). Daily chart negative-biased as MACD & stochastics in bearish mode. Support at 1.0311 (Friday's low, near 200-day moving average); breach would expose downside to 1.0242 (Aug. 12 low), then 1.0108 (Aug. 11 low) and 0.9924 (Aug. 9 reaction low). Resistance at 1.0481 (Friday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.0557 (Thursday's high), then 1.0601 (Wednesday's high), 1.0638 (61.8% Fibonacci correction of decline from July 27 high of 1.1080 to Aug. 9 low of 0.9924; near confluence of 55-day and 100-day moving averages) and 1.0785 (Aug. 3 high).\par \par \uc2 NZD/USD - to trade in lower range. Undermined by elevated investor risk aversion. But NZD/USD losses tempered by negative USD sentiment, NZD-USD yield gap, firmer commodity prices. Daily chart negative-biased as MACD & stochastics in bearish mode. Support at 0.8118 (hourly chart); breach would target 0.8061 (Aug. 10 low), then 0.7959 (Aug. 9 low) and 0.7854 (May 23 low). Resistance at 0.8288 (Friday's high), then at 0.8338 (hourly chart) and 0.8378 (Thursday's high); breach would target 0.8424 (Wednesday's high), then 0.8438 (Aug. 8 high), 0.8465 (Aug. 5 high) and 0.8503 (61.8% Fibonacci correction of decline from Aug. 1 high of 0.8840 to Aug. 9 low of 0.7959).\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD - to consolidate with risks skewed lower. Undermined by negative global risk sentiment, GBP sales on rebounding EUR/GBP cross. But GBP/USD losses tempered by negative USD sentiment, much-lower-than-expected UK July public sector net borrowing of just GBP20 million (vs forecast for GBP2.5 billion). Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics bearish at overbought; bearish shooting-star candlestick pattern completed Friday. Support at 1.6442 (Friday's low), then at 1.6419 (Thursday's low); breach would expose downside to 1.6353 (Wednesday's low), then 1.6321 (Tuesday's low), 1.6255 (Aug. 15 low), 1.6165 (Aug. 12 low) and 1.6109 (Aug. 11 low). Resistance at 1.6554 (hourly chart), then at 1.6618 (Friday's high); breach would expose upside to 1.6745 (April 28 top), then 1.6877 (Nov. 16, 2009 high), psychological 1.7000 and 1.7042 (Aug. 5, 2009 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/CHF - to consolidate. Undermined by flows to safe-haven CHF amid elevated investor risk aversion; weak USD sentiment. But USD/CHF downside limited by threat of drastic measures from \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  to thwart CHF strength. Daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics turned bearish at overbought. Resistance at 0.7921 (hourly chart), then at 0.7959 (Friday's high), 0.7991 (Thursday's high) and 0.8020 (Wednesday's high); breach would expose upside to 0.8048 (July 28 high), then 0.8129 (55-day moving average) and 0.8247 (July 22 high). Support at 0.7805 (Friday's low); breach would expose downside to 0.7767 (Tuesday's low), then 0.7548 (Aug. 12 low), 0.7237 (Aug. 11 low) and 0.7180 (Aug. 10 