\par\par \b \uc2 Record High Level For Yen Raises  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Stakes, Pressures BOJ\b0\par\par\uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2011\par 13:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Post-war high for yen raises stakes for another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Demand growing for BOJ to help with further easing measures\par \par \uc2 -- Tokyo trading rooms readying for early Monday action\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By William Sposato and Megumi Fujikawa \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A rise in the yen to a post-war record has markets ready for another round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as early as Monday morning and increased calls for the Bank of Japan to take fresh monetary easing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen hit a new high against the dollar in Friday trading in New York, capping a renewed rise since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  staged a record \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of around Y4.6 trillion on Aug. 4 to try to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower. The dollar dropped to Y75.94 after Takehiko Nakao, Japanese vice finance minister for international affairs, said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would take a measured approach to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although the dollar later recovered its losses to Y76.54 in late New York trade, analysts and traders said the pressure was on for the authorities to again wade into the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asked about the yen's strength, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda told NHK Television that he would "respond with sense of urgency in the new week." The Finance Ministry is responsible for deciding on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is then executed by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investors are fully ready for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ; we'll get set from Monday early morning," said Yuji Saito, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market director at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan's policymakers have sat on their hands since their failed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen earlier this month, contemplating what to do next," said Capital Economics in a report over the weekend. "It looks increasingly likely that they will be forced to act again sooner rather than later," the firm said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saito said Japan may make one concerted effort to bring the dollar back to Y80, although he said achieving such a large price swing would be costly, requiring massive volumes of yen selling.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be successful, the move would need to be accompanied by renewed action from the Bank of Japan, according to many political leaders and market analysts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ has a policy board meeting on Sept. 6-7, but could act sooner with an emergency meeting as it did last August shortly before the first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 6-1/2 years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sadakazu Tanigaki, head of the opposition Liberal Democratic Party, said on NHK Television on Sunday that the BOJ must play a role in helping to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This is something we have to think about. We must ask for serious discussions on whether another round of easing in monetary policy can be implemented," said Tanigaki, a former finance minister.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People familiar with the BOJ's thinking say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take further measures if necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ is ready to act swiftly if it confirms the high yen is starting to hurt business sentiment and threaten the BOJ's main economic scenario," said one person.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even though the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  does not have a role in exchange rates, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made clear that the high yen is a worry because of its impact on big industrial exporters and domestic job creation as jobs are shipped offshore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Among the limited policy options for the BOJ, the most likely new step would be a further expansion of its asset purchase program that buys a range of assets including government bonds and private-sector funds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said Japanese authorities will likely be watching the Tokyo stock market closely on Monday, to see if the strong yen is affecting the broader economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Nikkei Stock Average fell a steep 2.5% on Friday to a five-month closing low and is likely to come under renewed pressure when trading resumes after Friday's subsequent 1.6% fall in the Dow Industrials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa and William Sposato, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2785;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 william.sposato@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Yuka Hayashi and Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this article. [ 08-21-11 0718ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110821e78l00005\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
