\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  mulling another  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  - Nikkei\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2011\par 01:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Tokyo will mull \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on further yen gains - Nikkei\par \par \uc2 * BOJ may ease policy to boost yen-weakening effect\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, background)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again to stem further yen gains after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight ascent to a fresh record high against the dollar, the Nikkei newspaper said on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 If the yen continues to rise, Japanese authorities will step into the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and will seek understanding for its unilateral action from its Group of Seven counterparts, the paper said without citing sources.\par \par \uc2 Growing volatility in global markets has raised investors' appetite for safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the yen, pushing down the dollar to a record low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. It bounced back above 76 yen after falling below its previous record low of 76.25 set in March.\par \par \uc2 If yen rises persist, the Bank of Japan may also ease monetary policy to support government efforts to weaken the yen at its rate review next month or even earlier, sources familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking say.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange-rate market and eased monetary policy earlier this month, but the measures have not kept the yen from rising as investors seek the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a safe-haven against risk.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers have continued to issue verbal warnings of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem sharp yen gains since then, while the BOJ has signalled its readiness to ease further if sharp yen rises hurt business sentiment and threaten prospects of economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Some in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not rule out easing policy at an emergency meeting this month, although the chance of this is small unless yen gains are sharp enough to trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and are accompanied by big falls in Tokyo share prices.\par \par \uc2 But analysts have doubted whether such measures would be effective in countering broad dollar weakness in the market.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Jon Boyle)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NIKKEI (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110822e78j001ds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
