\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Sinks To Record Low Vs Yen Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risk\b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephen L. Bernard   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 610 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2011\par 23:11\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Unconvinced by the near constant risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders sent the dollar to a new record low against the yen Friday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell as low as Y75.94 before clawing back most of those losses. The dollar also weakened against the Swiss franc, though its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also looming over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with the possible threat of action.\par \par \uc2 There are "risks at these levels that the [\uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  or Bank of Japan] will step in over the weekend," said Omer Esiner, chief market analyst at \uc2 Commonwealth \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Washington. "It highlights the extent of how in demand the market is for safe havens."\par \par \uc2 Analysts say Friday's dollar drop below Y76 for the first time was likely pushed by technical triggers--when automatic trades set up around the previous record low of Y76.25 were hit, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair took a dive.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's consistent drop against the yen has pushed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  multiple times in recent months and forced government officials to talk tough about fighting the move, but so far they haven't been able to cause much more than a temporary pause in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this month only provided temporary relief. The country's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Japan might look to take more long-term steps to provide manufacturers stung by the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relief, including possible measures in the country's third supplementary budget.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy bureaucrat said that fundamentals were not driving demand for the yen, an oft-repeated piece of rhetoric. There's an element of speculation behind the trading, said Takehiko Nakao, vice finance minister for international affairs.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland is facing an eerily similar fate as investors pour into the franc and out of the dollar and euro. The strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hurt the countries' exporters who face competition in international markets from countries where goods are cheaper.\par \par \uc2 Both the U.S. and Europe are facing major economic questions and struggling under mounting debt, issues that have made the franc and yen unattractive options for investors.\par \par \uc2 Rumors have swirled for more than a week that the SNB might peg its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or at least narrow its trading range to a specific band against the euro to weaken the franc. Those threats weakened the franc for a short while, but it's already clear that investors are ramping up their one-way bets favoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.\par \par \uc2 The "SNB is reluctant to do the next step to take a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg or band," said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the SNB tried to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and lost a lot of money--analysts say that's kept the SNB from making any major new announcements.\par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the euro was at $1.4396 from $1.4334 late Thursday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y76.54 from Y76.57, while the euro was at Y110.20 from Y109.75. The U.K. pound was at $1.6479 from $1.6513. The dollar was at CHF0.7848 from CHF0.7941.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at about 73.990 from about 74.244.\par \par \uc2 - Tania Chen contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 -By Stephen L. Bernard, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-4528; stephen.bernard@dowjones.com [ 08-19-11 1711ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110819e78j0004w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
