\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK-Dollar drops but respite in sight if economy dims\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2011\par 18:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Dollar/yen plunges to record low\par \par \uc2 * Market eyes Fed Chairman Bernanke speech next week\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators increased bets against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Bank funding concerns rise, seen positive for dollar\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Julie Haviv\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Aug 19 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar plumbed a record low against the yen and weakened against the euro on Friday, but respite may be in sight for the greenback if the global economic landscape gets gloomier and feeds a safe-haven bid.\par \par \uc2 The euro has gained about 0.3 percent against the dollar so far in August while the greenback has lost around 1.2 percent versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the yen on Friday by a Wall Street Journal report cited Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official saying Japanese authorities do not plan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  often. [ID:nN1E77I0EC]\par \par \uc2 The dollar smashed through its previous record low of 76.25 set in March to fall below 76 yen <JPY=EBS> on trading platform EBS. The dollar later rebounded to trade 0.1 percent lower at 76.48 yen, marking a 5.8 percent loss so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Growing volatility in global markets has raised investors' appetite for the traditional safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 : the yen and Swiss franc. But there has been diminishing volatility in the yen, with its daily price action narrowing.\par \par \uc2 "That speaks to the ongoing worries over the situation and isn't something the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own can resolve by a wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Andrew Wilkinson, senior market analyst at Interactive Brokers in Greenwich, Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 Investors are awaiting Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's speech on Aug. 26 in Jackson Hole, Wyoming, for hints on how policymakers plan to handle the turmoil in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's annual Jackson Hole meeting last year was when the Fed hinted at plans for a second round of quantitative easing, which sent the dollar on a downward trek.\par \par \uc2 Didi Weinblatt, vice president of mutual fund portfolios at USAA Investments in San Antonio, Texas, was pessimistic about any efforts to stimulate the economy.\par \par \uc2 "There is really not much more the Fed can do because interest rates are already as low as they can get," she said. "There is a lot of nervousness, some of which is coming from Europe and I do not see any good solutions."\par \par \uc2 Weinblatt, who oversees about $4 billion in assets, said she has been eyeing purchasing high quality, high yield corporate bonds, but said U.S. Treasuries are too expensive.\par \par \uc2 "Whatever happens, the U.S. dollar should remain supported by the fact that there is really no alternative to its liquidity and safety," she said.\par \par \uc2 Next week's U.S. economic calendar is on the light side, with the highlight likely to be the second estimate of second-quarter gross domestic product on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Bill Gross\uc2 , co-chief investment officer of \uc2 Pacific Investment Management Co\uc2 ., operator of the world's largest bond fund, said the rally in Treasury yields to 60-year lows reflects a high probability of recession in the United States. [ID:nN1E77I0ZE] For more from the Interview, please click on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://insider.thomsonreuters.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://insider.thomsonreuters.com/}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon New York trading, the euro was up 0.4 percent against the dollar on the day at $1.4392 <EUR=>.\par \par \uc2 The euro was also boosted by market chatter that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying peripheral bonds [GVD/EUR].\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators increased bets against the U.S. dollar, according to data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission released on Friday. [ID:nN1E77I153]\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc also rose on Friday, although gains were capped by speculation that Swiss authorities will step in again to rein in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar was last down 1 percent at 0.7856 franc <CHF=>. The euro <EURCHF=> was down 0.6 percent against the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.1308 francs, having earlier fallen roughly 1 percent in choppy trade.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts expect the dollar, which has also struggled due to U.S. fiscal problems, will be supported on the view that demand for the greenback will rise if signs grow that financial institutions may be facing funding problems.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss and Nick Olivari; Editing by Leslie Adler)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 10)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110819e78j0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
