\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NODA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , MONETARY EASING PREFERRED \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MEASURES FOR NOW \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister said Friday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and monetary easing are preferred measures in the short-term, but if the yen stabilizes around its current levels, extra measures may be considered in the third supplementary budget. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA 2Q REAL HOUSEHOLD INCOME UP 0.5% ON YEAR VS DOWN 0.9% IN 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's real average household income rose for the first time in three quarters during the April-June period as private sector hiring conditions continued to improve, data from Statistics Korea showed Friday. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: CHINA SHOULD PREPARE FOR US QE3 CONSEQUENCES - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should be prepared for more hot-money inflows and greater inflationary pressures which may result from a third round of U.S. quantitative easing, the National Business Daily reported Friday, citing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser Li Daokui. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: EXPECTS ADJUSTMENT IN MONETARY TIGHTENING POLICY IN CURRENT HALF--REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China could see some structural adjustment in the monetary tightening measures in the current half of the year, including "selective easing," the Shanghai Securities News reported Friday, citing a researcher with a government think tank. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA THINK TANK RESEARCHER: SOME CURBS ON PROPERTY MARKET ARE EXCESSIVE - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some of China's measures to curb price increases in the property market are excessive, the Financial News reported Friday, citing the head of a government think tank. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TRADE MIN KAIEDA: IN TALKS WITH DPJ MEMBERS OVER POSSIBLE LEADERSHIP CANDIDACY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's industry minister Banri Kaieda said Friday he in talks with other members of the ruling Democratic Party of Japan about the possibility of running for head of the party. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDONESIA JULY NEW CAR SALES 89,056 UNITS VS 70,156 IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New car sales in Indonesia in July rose 27% to 89,056 units from 70,157 units a month earlier, Indonesia's car manufacturer association Gaikindo said Friday. (published 0113 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI GOVT OFFERS INCENTIVES TO FIRST-TIME HOME, CAR BUYERS -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai government plans to provide incentives for first-time buyers of homes and cars, The Nation reported Friday, citing Deputy Finance Minister Boonsong Teriyapirom. (published 0254 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED'S FISHER: US GOING TO HAVE A POSITIVE THIRD QUARTER - CNBC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Richard Fisher\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the president of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Friday there will be growth in the third quarter of 2011 in the U.S., but said it will be a "slow slog" for the world's biggest economy. (published 2359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: RENEWED FEARS EUROPE'S BANKS TOO WEAK TO WITHSTAND DEBT CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A dramatic sell-off in European financial markets on Thursday renewed fears that Europe's banks are too weak to withstand the Continent's debt crisis, increasing the chances that the region's leaders will be forced to pursue radical steps toward fiscal union in order to preserve their single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0024 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: EURO-BOND PROPOSAL COMES WITH STEEP POLITICAL COST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is keeping financing flowing to Italy, Spain and the euro zone's other weak countries by buying their government bonds in the open market. (published 0028 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIR NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2 : CONSIDERING NZ$150 MILLION BOND OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that it was considering a NZ$150 million offering of Nov. 15, 2016, bonds to the New Zealand market. (published 0123 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INDORAMA VENTURES BOARD OKS PLAN TO ISSUE UP TO THB25 BLN BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The board of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indorama Ventures PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a Thai plastics and polyester producer, has approved a plan to issue up to THB25 billion worth of bonds. (published 0145 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S QUEENSLAND STATE LEFT BEHIND IN RUSH TO SAFETY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the global rush to safety, Australia's Queensland state is being left behind. Amid a concerning mix of U.S. economic data and escalating worries in recent days about European banks' access to funding, Australian government debt has been touted as a new safe-haven asset. (published 0236 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: LOW RATES HIT MONEY-MARKET FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Money-market mutual funds, those havens of safety for investors during tumultuous times, are facing their own pressures as interest rates continue to decline. (published 0123 GMT) [ 19-08-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110819e78j0006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
