\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Fin Min Noda:  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Must Have Surprise Element\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2011\par 11:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 05:51 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: If Deficit-Covering Bond Bill Isn't Passed, Will Affect Econ From Oct\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 05:57 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Corp Tax Cut Needed To Prevent Cos Leaving Japan For Oversees\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:02 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Continue To Watch Market Carefully, Take Decisive Action When Necessary\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:09 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Current Generation Must Bear Burden Of Reconstruction\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:11 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Must Consider Reconstruction Funding From Core Taxes - Income, Consumption, Corp Taxes\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:14 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: 3rd Supplementary Budget Should Consider Measures To Aid Those Suffering From High Yen\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:16 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: 3rd Supplementary Budget Should Include Incentives To Keep Jobs, Aid For Small Businesses\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:19 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Govt Debt Ratio Could Trigger Something Worse Than High Yen\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:30 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Must Not Use Disaster As Excuse To Step Back From Fiscal Discipline\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:37 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Cooperation With Oppposition, Including Grand Coalition, Should Be Considered\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:39 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: Some Call For BOJ Underwriting Of Govt Bonds But That Is Prohibited\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:53 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda: BOJ Should Continue To Support Econ With More Easing If Needed\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 06:59 EDT *DJ  Japan Noda Was Giving A Speech At A Dinner Near Tokyo\par \par \uc2 18 Aug 2011 07:35 EDT DJ  Japan Noda: Must Not Use Disaster As Excuse To Step Back From Fiscal Discipline\par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's finance minister said Thursday that the government must not use reconstruction from the March 11 disasters as an excuse to back away from fiscal discipline.\par \par \uc2 "The burden for disaster reconstruction should be shouldered by the current generation," Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said in a speech to a non-profit organization.\par \par \uc2 "We must not use the disaster as an excuse to move away from fiscal discipline," he said.\par \par \uc2 Noting that Japan has the highest debt-to-GDP ratio among major industrialized countries, Noda said any consideration of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  underwriting government bond sales to finance reconstruction is "a prohibited strategy."\par \par \uc2 "Nobody wants to raises taxes," he said, adding "we must have a sustainable system, otherwise we will be like the EU and the U.S.," referring to recent debt crises in those areas.\par \par \uc2 Noda, who is considered the leading candidate to succeed outgoing Prime Minister Naoto Kan, said he would continue talking to opposition parties about a "grand coalition" to gain the necessary cooperation to tackle difficult issues.\par \par \uc2 He suggested a new government should bring opposition members into the Cabinet to realize fuller cross-party cooperation.\par \par \uc2 Kan is expected to resign at the end of next week after the passage of two key bills through parliament. A leadership race for the governing Democratic Party Of Japan is set to be held by the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 -By Toko Sekiguchi, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2787; toko.sekiguchi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 18, 2011 07:35 ET (11:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110818e78i002zs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
