\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Up On Firm Share Prices; Trade Volume Thin\b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2011\par 07:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Euro gains due to firm regional shares\par \par \uc2 -- Holiday-thinned Tokyo market helps magnify euro's gain\par \par \uc2 -- Euro may rise more if Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  takes further action to weaken franc\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar fall toward Y75 still possible, analysts say\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The euro rose against the dollar and the yen Monday in Asia as firm regional share prices prompted investors to buy the risk-sensitive high-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market participants took a cue from Japan's benchmark Nikkei 225 Stock Average, which was up 1.24% as of 0450 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro-buying wasn't that aggressive, but the impact of these orders was magnified due to Tokyo's thin trading volume, traders said. Many Japanese investors take summer leave around this time of the year, a period called obon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's almost like a Saturday market," said a senior dealer at a major Japanese bank. "An investor buys $10 million for example, which is a small amount for the market, but rates would move by 10 to 20 points."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the euro was at Y109.79 from Y109.32 on Friday in New York and was at $1.4294 from $1.4250 last week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Looking ahead, the dealer said the euro may rise further if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  takes further steps to weaken the Swiss franc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We cannot miss any SNB actions for the time being, and if the SNB takes more steps, the euro will reap the most benefit," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar, meanwhile, was at Y76.81 from Y76.72. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 74.463 from 74.565.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists said the dollar still faces the risk of a decline toward Y75.00, well below its post-war record of Y76.25.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief Japan strategist Masafumi Yamamoto said the downward pressure on the dollar remains as the Fed is unlikely to change its easy-policy stance for the time being.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And Citibank Japan chief strategist Osamu Takashima said it became a bit harder for Japan to step into the market than it was last week because share prices are now rising.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's now a bit harder for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to find an excuse to conduct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            76.81-82       76.82-88  -0.05    77.09    76.80  -5.31 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.4293-96      1.4265-70  +0.19   1.4316   1.4258  +6.75 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.6281-86      1.6274-82  +0.03   1.6304   1.6274  +4.33 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.7887-94      0.7831-38  +0.71   0.7914   0.7822 -15.61 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9873-78      0.9906-08  -0.32   0.9905   0.9866  -0.72 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0414-18      1.0350