\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Yen Plunges As BOJ Rattles Nerves\b0\par\par\uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 11:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Yen's sharp moves spark \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert\par \par \uc2 --Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  not behind the moves, traders say\par \par \uc2 --Pressure rising on Japanese authorities to take action to stem yen strength\par \par \uc2 (Adds further details, background and comment throughout.)\par \par \uc2 By Clare Connaghan\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The chances of fresh official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen increased Thursday, as the Bank of Japan spooked traders into hammering the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by checking their rates.\par \par \uc2 Several traders said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  contacted them to check their levels for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --a move that often signals an imminent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With the yen hovering close to historic highs against the dollar, that was enough to spark a rapid selloff.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't sell yen itself, several dealers said. As a result, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly snapped back, with the dollar sliding from its peak of Y77.30 to Y76.49 by 0820 GMT.\par \par \uc2 See a chart of the yen's move against the dollar:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/5672"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/5672 }}}\par \par \uc2 "If it were an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar would have shot up much, much more," said one trader, who did not wish to be named.\par \par \uc2 Mitsuro Sakurai, a senior official at the Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , declined to comment on Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to calm markets on the MOF's behalf last week, buying $52 billion in an effort to push the yen down, citing "one-sided" moves that were pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  away from fundamental drivers. It worked, but only briefly, with the yen quickly rebounding.\par \par \uc2 The problem: a strong urge among investors to sell dollars and seek safety in highly uncertain times. Fresh clear signals from the U.S. Federal Reserve Tuesday that it intends to hold interest rates close to zero until 2013 added further fuel to the buck's decline against the yen.\par \par \uc2 Market-watchers still see a fresh sting as inevitable. In that environment, rate checks are enough to spark hefty short-term moves.\par \par \uc2 "A BOJ rate check just when it looked like the dollar was about to break its record low Y76.25 could certainly pack a punch like that," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Longer term, however, a stronger tool may be needed.\par \par \uc2 "If they're serious about trying to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation, they will have to come back in, but it's going to be a test of the BOJ's resolve," said Lee Hardman, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ in London.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the pressure is the fact that the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  announced a series of fresh measures Wednesday to counter Swiss franc strength, effectively chanelling extra safe-haven flows into the yen.\par \par \uc2 "After the SNB's steps yesterday, the onus is now on the BOJ," Hardman said.\par \par \uc2 Export-denting yen strength has clouded the outlook for Japan's export-driven economy as it recovers from the March 11 earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 -By Clare Connaghan, Dow Jones Newswires; +44 (0) 20 7842 9496, clare.connaghan@dowjones.com (Katie Martin and Eva Salay contributed to this article)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 11, 2011 05:12 ET (09:12 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110811e78b002rm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
