\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : BOJ Presence Spooks Markets, Euro Off Highs\b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 13:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Bank of Japan checks prices in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, spooks traders\par \par \uc2 --Yen plunges briefly, but regains losses almost immediately\par \par \uc2 --Euro off highs as French bank worries resurface\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eva Szalay \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were on high alert for another round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a brief but dramatic plunge in the yen in early European trading, while the euro fell back from session highs as French banking worries resurfaced, knocking stocks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen sank some 1.3% against the dollar to trade as high as Y77.30 from Y76.30 as the BOJ checked prices in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, but quickly regained most of those losses to trade around Y76.51.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the BOJ refrained from actively \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets this time, but the fact it was checking prices spooked investors into liquidating yen long positions just in case.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market watchers said they expect a fresh round of yen selling by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  very soon. "If they're serious about trying to stop the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation, they will have to come back in, but it's going to be a test of the BOJ's resolve," said Lee Hardman, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  UFJ in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ last week spent around $52 billion buying dollars against the yen in an effort to cap the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's appreciation, but the move failed to have a lasting impact as global economic growth concerns and heightened fiscal worries in the U.S. and Europe spurred investors to seek shelter in safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  like the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adding to the pressure was the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's announcement of fresh policy measures Wednesday to counter Swiss franc strength, effectively channeling extra safe-haven flows into the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "After the SNB's steps yesterday, the onus is now on the BOJ," Hardman said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro traded in positive territory against the dollar for much of the session as equity markets bounced after Wednesday's sharp losses, but later fell back as French banking stocks led a retreat in choppy trading conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The cost of insuring debt issued by European banks at one point rose to a fresh record high.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was again purchasing Spanish and Italian bonds, but the move failed to have much of an impact on the euro.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "A week ago, the market wanted [the ECB] to buy Italian and Spanish debt... But markets are still waiting for the implementation of the [European Financial Stability Facility changes] in Europe, with purchases by the Securities Market Program seen as a temporary measure," said Steven Saywell, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In emerging markets, Central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under heavy pressure overnight, but trimmed losses in London trading hours.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1045 GMT, the euro was at $1.4178 compared with $1.4176 late Wednesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y76.59 from Y76.85, while the euro was at Y108.61 from Y108.95. Earlier, the cross mimicked the dollar's move against the yen, with the euro trading as high as Y109.89 from Y108.66, before paring its losses. The U.K. pound was at $1.6137 from $1.6130. The dollar was at CHF0.7406 from CHF0.7265.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was around 74.769 from about 74.779.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1033 GMT     1.4186     76.59      1.6143     0.7387 \par 3 Day Trend       Range      Bearish    Bearish    Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Range      Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.4032     81.73      1.6091     0.8928 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4402     77.30      1.6326     0.7480 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4335     76.99      1.6281     0.7420 \par 1st Resistance    1.4275     76.65      1.6204     0.7404 \par Pivot*            1.4247     76.87      1.6192     0.7260 \par 1st Support       1.4158     76.44      1.6114     0.7318 \par 2nd Support       1.4122     76.25      1.6092     0.7271 \par 3rd Support       1.4055     75.68      1.6040     0.7236 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/JPY \par  \par Spot 1033 GMT     108.69 \par 3 Day Trend       Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bearish \par 200 day