\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Options Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 04:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Dollar/yen options rose sharply in Asia Thursday as investors stocked up hedging contracts against another possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Benchmark one-month at-the-money implied volatilities stood at 13.85%/14.55% as of 0200GMT, much higher than 12.60%/13.30% in the previous day in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 Asian investors are interested in short-term dollar-call contracts which make money on the greenback's surge. One example is a one-week contract with a Y78 strike, and the reason behind the popularity is speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may conduct an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 In Asian Thursday session, the greenback is traded around Y76.50, close to its post-war record low of Y76.25 and below Y77.10 where Japan stepped into the market last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Still, options dealers haven't been able to buy contracts so far "because many market participants are on the buying side," a senior options dealer at a Japanese bank said.\par \par \uc2 He added volatilities will keep rising as they expect the market "will remain volatile."\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    1 Month Option Implied Volatilities At 0200 GMT \par  \par               Tokyo           Tokyo \par               Thursday        Wednesday \par Dollar/Yen    13.85%/14.55%   12.60%/13.30% \par Euro/Dollar   15.15%/15.40%   14.55%/14.80% \par Euro/Yen      17.95%/18.95%   16.75%/17.75% \par  \par  \par    3 Month Option Implied Volatilities \par  \par               Tokyo          Tokyo \par               Thursday       Wednesday \par Dollar/Yen    13.05%/13.65%  12.20%/12.80% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volatilities used are over-the-counter, at-the-money rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1-month 25 delta risk-reversals favor dollar put/yen call options by 1.75%/2.25% compared with 1.75%/2.25% in Tokyo Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 11-08-11 0232GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1077 4127   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110811e78b0007d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
