up spending hit by the March 11 earthquake and tsunami, though global economic jitters are clouding the outlook for corporate investment as a strong yen prods more companies to move production overseas.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY'S BABACAN: 2011 CURRENT ACCOUNT GAP TO BE LESS THAN 10% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's current account deficit will be less than 10% of gross domestic product by the end of the year and the government will shortly announce measures to narrow the gap, Deputy Prime Minister Ali Babacan said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWEDEN FIN MINISTRY: WILL HAVE TO REVISE 2012 GDP FORECAST LOWER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden's finance ministry Thursday said the Swedish government will have to make a downwards revision of Sweden's 2012 gross domestic product forecast, due to the economic turbulence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UK DEPUTY PM: CONFIDENT THAT POLICE CUTS ARE MANAGEABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. Deputy Prime Minister Nick Clegg gave his backing to Prime Minister David Cameron on the need for cuts to police spending Thursday, despite concerns that large numbers of officers were needed to cope with the rioting in London and other English cities this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YEN'S LEVEL, NOT SPEED, DECIDING FACTOR FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A concern that the recent strong level of the yen would take hold in the market was what led Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda to order last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting that the authorities are ready to act again, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES TO 16.6% IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's unemployment rate jumped to a new record high in May, as the army of jobless workers swelled to more than 822,000, the country's statistics agency said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK REPOSSESSION ORDERS DECLINE IN SECOND QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. courts granted fewer orders for repossession against homeowners who have fallen behind in their mortgage payments in the second quarter of 2011 compared with the first, official data showed Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF SAKURAI: GOVT MAY HAVE TO TAKE BUDGET STEPS TO SOFTEN YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior official from Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday the government would have to take budgetary stimulus steps to soften the impact of the yen's rises on the economy if an analysis of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength suggests such action is needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YUAN HITS FRESH HIGH VS DOLLAR; GAINS ACCELERATE ON INFLATION FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan rose against the U.S. dollar to another high Thursday, boosting regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely tied to the Chinese economy and reinforcing the perception that Beijing is allowing the yuan to play a key role in containing high inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NO REASON TO THINK SPAIN'S GROWTH WILL CEASE - GOVERNMENT SPOKESMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is no reason to think Spain's timid economic recovery will come to an end this year despite a more challenging global environment, the chief government spokesman said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC INJECTS NET CNY70 BLN INTO MARKET AMID GLOBAL FINANCIAL TURMOIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  injected a net CNY70 billion into the money market this week through its open-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in an apparent move to keep liquidity flush in the domestic market amid the global financial turmoil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY JUNE CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT NARROWS TO $7.55B VS $7.76B IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's current-account deficit more than doubled on the year in June to $7.55 billion, broadly in line with economists' expectations, following a $7.76 billion deficit in May.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT EDANO: MULLING ECON MEASURES IF GLOBAL MALAISE CONTINUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's top spokesman said Thursday that the government may take domestic economic measures to help those affected by the volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: YEN MOVES CONTINUE TO BE ONE-SIDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister vowed Thursday he will closely watch the yen, calling its recent moves toward a record high versus the dollar "one-sided."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TO CUT FISCAL 2011 ECONOMIC GROWTH FORECAST TO AROUND 0.5% -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government is set to downwardly revise its projection for Japan's economic growth in fiscal 2011 to around 0.5%, Kyodo News reported Thursday, citing officials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWISS NATIONAL BANK JORDAN: EVALUATING A RANGE OF MEASURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is evaluating a range of measures to stall the Swiss franc's rise, and doesn't exclude moves that affect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said in a newspaper interview Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN JOBLESS RATE RISE ADD TO RATE CUT CHATTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's unemployment rate rose for the first time since mid-2010 in July, confirming that conditions in parts of the economy not exposed to the mining boom have slowedb down. The fall could raise chances of a possible cut in interest rates by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or RBA, especially if global markets remain on edge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CURRENT EVENTS GIVE OPPORTUNITY TO BOOST YUAN FLEXIBILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should use current turmoil in international markets as an opportunity to boost the flexibility of its exchange rate, a Chinese government scholar said in an essay distributed Thursday. )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC PROFESSOR: NOT A GOOD TIME TO RAISE INTEREST RATES -PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's authorities should tolerate high inflation for a while and try not to increase interest rates given the complicated global and domestic economic environment, an academic with China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  wrote in a commentary piece on Thursday. [ 08-11-11 0611ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110811e78b00026\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
