\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,181 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2011\par 12:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB: FORECASTERS RAISE INFLATION OUTLOOK FOR 2011, 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Professional forecasters have increased their expectations for inflation this year and next, the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reported Thursday in its Monthly Bulletin. This change in outlook may cast doubt on some economists' expectations that the ECB would slow policy tightening, or even cut rates soon.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK HOLDS RATE STEADY; CAUTIOUS ABOUT FUTURE HIKES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea left its benchmark interest rate unchanged for a second straight month as it treads cautiously to normalize policy amid global market turmoil and concerns about the health of major export markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ECB BUYS ITALIAN, SPANISH BONDS FOR FOURTH DAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought Italian and Spanish bonds Thursday, a trader said, maintaining the presence in the market for the fourth consecutive day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ITALY'S TREMONTI OUTLINES BALANCED BUDGET RULE, ECONOMIC REFORM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian Economy Minister Giulio Tremonti Thursday urged members of parliament to make a balanced-budget amendment part of the country's constitution, emphasizing that current fiscal rules "haven't been a success" as they led to the country's "extraordinary" burden of EUR1.9 trillion in public debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IRISH JULY CPI ROSE 2.7% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Irish consumer prices rose 2.7% in July from a year earlier, driven by increases in home loan interest rates, and higher costs for water, gas and electricity, the Irish government said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EU, IMF POSITIVE ON PORTUGAL'S BAILOUT WORK - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials from the European Union and the International Monetary Fund are expected to give a positive first review of Portugal's implementation of a EUR78 billion bailout program, a person familiar with the situation said Thursday. (published 1109 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANKS TURN INCREASINGLY TO ECB BORROWING AS FEARS MOUNT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Use of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's overnight deposit facility jumped to its highest level in three months Wednesday, amid market rumors that French lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  was close to failure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MACHINERY ORDERS UP, BUT GLOBAL JITTERS CLOUD OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders rose briskly in June as firms dialed up spending hit by the March 11 earthquake and tsunami, though global economic jitters are clouding the outlook for corporate investment as a strong yen prods more companies to move production overseas.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY'S BABACAN: 2011 CURRENT ACCOUNT GAP TO BE LESS THAN 10% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's current account deficit will be less than 10% of gross domestic product by the end of the year and the government will shortly announce measures to narrow the gap, Deputy Prime Minister Ali Babacan said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWEDEN FIN MINISTRY: WILL HAVE TO REVISE 2012 GDP FORECAST LOWER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden's finance ministry Thursday said the Swedish government will have to make a downwards revision of Sweden's 2012 gross domestic product forecast, due to the economic turbulence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UK DEPUTY PM: CONFIDENT THAT POLICE CUTS ARE MANAGEABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. Deputy Prime Minister Nick Clegg gave his backing to Prime Minister David Cameron on the need for cuts to police spending Thursday, despite concerns that large numbers of officers were needed to cope with the rioting in London and other English cities this week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YEN'S LEVEL, NOT SPEED, DECIDING FACTOR FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A concern that the recent strong level of the yen would take hold in the market was what led Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda to order last week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting that the authorities are ready to act again, people familiar with the matter said. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK UNEMPLOYMENT RATE RISES TO 16.6% IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's unemployment rate jumped to a new record high in May, as the army of jobless workers swelled to more than 822,000, the country's statistics agency said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK REPOSSESSION ORDERS DECLINE IN SECOND QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. courts granted fewer orders for repossession against homeowners who have fallen behind in their mortgage payments in the second quarter of 2011 compared with the first, official data showed Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF SAKURAI: GOVT MAY HAVE TO TAKE BUDGET STEPS TO SOFTEN YEN'S RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior official from Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Thursday the government would have to take budgetary stimulus steps to soften the impact of the yen's rises on the economy if an analysis of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength suggests such action is needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YUAN HITS FRESH HIGH VS DOLLAR; GAINS ACCELERATE ON INFLATION FIGHT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan rose against the U.S. dollar to another high Thursday, boosting regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely tied to the Chinese economy and reinforcing the perception that Beijing is allowing the yuan to play a key role in containing high inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NO REASON TO THINK SPAIN'S GROWTH WILL CEASE - GOVERNMENT SPOKESMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There is no reason to think Spain's timid economic recovery will come to an end this year despite a more challenging global environment, the chief government spokesman said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC INJECTS NET CNY70 BLN INTO MARKET AMID GLOBAL FINANCIAL TURMOIL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  injected a net CNY70 billion into the money market this week through its open-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in an apparent move to keep liquidity flush in the domestic market amid the global financial turmoil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TURKEY JUNE CURRENT ACCOUNT DEFICIT NARROWS TO $7.55B VS $7.76B IN MAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's current-account deficit more than doubled on the year in June to $7.55 billion, broadly in line with economists' expectations, following a $7.76 billion deficit in May.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT EDANO: MULLING ECON MEASURES IF GLOBAL MALAISE CONTINUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government's top spokesman said Thursday that the government may take domestic economic measures to help those affected by the volatile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: YEN MOVES CONTINUE TO BE ONE-SIDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Minister vowed Thursday he will closely watch the yen, calling its recent moves toward a record high versus the dollar "one-sided."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN TO CUT FISCAL 2011 ECONOMIC GROWTH FORECAST TO AROUND 0.5% -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government is set to downwardly revise its projection for Japan's economic growth in fiscal 2011 to around 0.5%, Kyodo News reported Thursday, citing officials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SWISS NATIONAL BANK JORDAN: EVALUATING A RANGE OF MEASURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is evaluating a range of measures to stall the Swiss franc's rise, and doesn't exclude moves that affect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said in a newspaper interview Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par      ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par FOCUS: TRADERS BET ON ECB RATE CUT, UK EASING AS GROWTH SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The faltering global economic recovery and brittle risk sentiment are prompting investors to price in rate cuts by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , just one month after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lifted rates to temper inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: PBOC ADVISER: CHINA WILLING TO KEEP BUYING EUROPE, US DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China is willing to keep buying the sovereign debt of the U.S. and European nations, but those countries need to commit to long-term reforms that "really alter the declining trend" in their fiscal health, Li Daokui, an adviser of the People's Bank of China, said Thursday. [ 11-08-11 1057GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020110811e78b0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
