\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Japanese economy still poised to pick up despite strong yen\b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2011\par 14:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll data click on <ECONPOLL1> or [ECILT/PDF]\par \par \uc2 * Japan's economy to rebound in Q3, then grow moderately\par \par \uc2 * Strong yen poses risks to exports\par \par \uc2 * More \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , further BOJ easing possible\par \par \uc2 By Kaori Kaneko\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Japan's economy will recover in the latter half of this fiscal year despite growing worries about the global economy and the yen's continued strength even after\par \par \uc2 official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a Reuters poll shows.\par \par \uc2 The world's third-biggest economy will emerge from recession this quarter and is expected to grow moderately thereafter, according to a poll of 50 economists taken over the past week.\par \par \uc2 Gross domestic product will grow 1.2 percent in the current quarter, the median estimate of the poll conducted from Aug. 2-8 showed, largely in line with a 1.1 percent expansion foreca st made in the July poll.\par \par \uc2 The expansion would follow a 0.7 percent contraction in April-June, unchanged from the July forecast and the third straight quarterly contraction.\par \par \uc2 But the strong yen could squeeze Japanese exporters' profits, and worries about the outlook for the euro zone and U.S. debt problems are making investors cautious, leading some anal ysts to warn they could trim their growth forecasts later this year.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment, the economy is expected to recover steadily within the fiscal year on the back of an improvement in supply constraints and post-quake reconstruction demand," said\par \par \uc2 Shuji Tonouchi, a senior fixed-income strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities.\par \par \uc2 "But if the yen stays strong, it could weigh on export growth. In that case, we may trim our economic growth forecast for the second half of this fiscal year."\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's strength and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy last week to ease pressure on the export-reliant economy after the yen spik ed close to a record high. [ID:nL3E7J41YW]\par \par \uc2 But ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warned on Monday that Tokyo's efforts to weaken the yen were ineffective and negative for its sovereign credit ratings, and a Reuters poll last wee k forecast safe-haven demand would keep the yen at high levels. [ID:nL3E7J70EG] [ID:nL3E7J33L9]\par \par \uc2 Big Japanese manufacturers estimate the average dollar/yen <JPY=> rate for the current fiscal year at 82.59 yen, the Bank of Japan's business sentiment survey showed last mo nth. But the yen is now stronger than 80.00 to the dollar, trading at 76.991 to the dollar on Tuesday. [JPBCLG=ECI]\par \par \uc2 Following Standard and Poor's downgrade of the United States' credit rating and as tensions in the euro zone debt market heightened, the Group of Seven nations on Monday p ledged to take coordinated action to ensure liquidity and to support financial markets' functioning, financial stability and economic growth. [ID:nN1E7760B4]\par \par \uc2 "The possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing policy further is still there," said Yoshimasa Maruyama, chief economist at\par \par \uc2 Itochu Economic Research Institute.\par \par \uc2 "If the dollar is sold sharply, not only against the yen but also against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we cannot deny a possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 With economic recovery expected, analysts held their projection that the Bank of Japan will keep its overnight call rate target near zero at least until the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 Japan's consumer inflation is forecast at 0.4 percent in this fiscal year to March 2012 and 0.3 percent in the next fiscal year, the poll showed, unchanged from the July survey.\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the poll click on [ID:nL6E7J81C8])\par \par \uc2 (Polling by Bangalore Polling Unit; Editing by Susan Fenton)\par \par \uc2 (kaori.kaneko@thomsonreuters.com Reuters Messaging:kaori.kaneko.reuters.com@reuters.net +81-3-6441-198)\par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110812e78900131\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
