\par\par \b \uc2 HIGHLIGHTS 2-Key quotes from Japan policymakers on yen, BOJ\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2011\par 05:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 9 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always ready to take monetary policy action when needed to support the economy, focusing on risks to the recovery posed by the yen's rise and the global slowdown.\par \par \uc2  Below are key quotes from Japanese policymakers on Tuesday in the wake of steep falls in global share prices and persistent rises in the yen:\par \par \uc2  BOJ GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, in parliament:\par \par \uc2  "We see a stronger need to focus on risks to Japan's economy ... In the short term, yen rises hurt exports and have a negative impact on Japan's economy. We're now experiencing broad dollar weakness. We need to think about what is driving this dollar weakness ...\par \par \uc2  "It's happening against the backdrop of weakness in the global economic recovery, and uncertainty over U.S. and European fiscal problems. These factors, coupled with the short-term downside effect from yen rises, hurt sentiment."\par \par \uc2  (Asked how the Fed's policy will affect Japan)\par \par \uc2  "I won't comment on the monetary policy of other central banks and how that will affect exchange-rate moves ... The BOJ is always ready to take appropriate action when needed.\par \par \uc2  "We have a strong sense of concern over recent yen rises. Last week we eased monetary policy taking into account various uncertainties, and we think we took sufficient measures.\par \par \uc2  "What we're seeing now is broad dollar weakness. I hope to urge other nations to take measures to reduce uncertainty over the global economy, which is the root cause of the current dollar weakness."\par \par \uc2  FINANCE MINISTER YOSHIHIKO NODA, to reporters:\par \par \uc2  (Asked about the stock market plunge, the yen's rise)\par \par \uc2  "I will pay close attention to market movements with a sense of urgency today."\par \par \uc2  NODA in parliament:\par \par \uc2  (Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week)\par \par \uc2  "The yen's rise was one-sided ... We judged it would have adverse effects on Japan's economy and financial system."\par \par \uc2  (Asked if there was a gap in how \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other nations saw the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the G7 teleconference)\par \par \uc2  "Markets are in a severe state, so we hope to communicate closely and take appropriate action as G7 ... We did not have any specific discussion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy ... But when there is a need, we will cooperate as appropriate."\par \par \uc2  (Asked if Tokyo waited too long before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 )\par \par \uc2  "We decided to step in because yen moves were becoming too one-sided. But we also felt the need to see the outcome of U.S. negotiations to meet the Aug. 2 deadline (for raising its debt ceiling)."\par \par \uc2  BOJ BOARD MEMBER SHIRAI, in parliament:\par \par \uc2  "The BOJ is pumping a massive amount of money into markets with its comprehensive monetary easing. Funds from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would add to that huge fund supply. The BOJ uses (yen sold via \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) as part of its massive fund supply to the market ...\par \par \uc2  "I'm very worried about the yen's excessive rise because it is happening just when Japan is restoring supply chains (disrupted by the March earthquake)."\par \par \uc2  CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY YUKIO EDANO, in news conference:\par \par \uc2  "Financial markets are determined by several different factors, and I'm not going to comment on each and every one of those factors. I will say that market moves could potentially impact the economy, so I want to monitor market moves closely." \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara, Rie Ishiguro, Tetsushi Kajimoto and Stanley White; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN (HIGHLIGHTS)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110812e78900060\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
