\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Suffers Brunt Of Massive High-Yield  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Selloff\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew J. Johnson   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2011\par 23:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--It was the euro, not the dollar, that bore the brunt of \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  downgrade of the U.S. credit rating to double-A-plus Monday. Rattled traders ran to the Swiss franc and the yen, abandoning riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  more closely tied to economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The euro was the focal point of a massive move away from nearly all higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at one point trading down as much as 3% against the safe-harbor Swiss franc, hitting a new all-time low of CHF1.0619. The dollar and U.K. pound also hit new all-time lows against the franc, though their declines were milder.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts believe the euro is still stronger than it should be, given that most of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains came on projections of strong global economic growth. With the U.S. potentially slipping back into recession, and even emerging markets showing some signs of slower expansion, the euro could stand to drop to its true value estimated of $1.20, rather than Monday's $1.42.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone's debt problems also appear to be worsening, further undermining the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Monday, French credit-default swaps widened significantly on fears that France also faces a downgrade from its triple-A rating. Traders view such a development as possibly the next serious stress point for the euro zone because France's triple-A rating helps back a triple-A rated European Financial Stability Facility. That fund is viewed as an essential emergency bailout fund for the euro zone's most vulnerable economies should they run into fresh troubles.\par \par \uc2 "The French AAA underpins the AAA rating of the [European Financial Stability Facility] and any downgrade would put the entire rescue mechanism in question," said Steven Englander, head of G10 strategy at \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 That French news overwhelmed news that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought Italian and Spanish bonds for the first time, driving yields on Italian and Spanish debt sharply lower.\par \par \uc2 Late Monday, the euro was at $1.4180 from $1.4275 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y77.79 from Y78.42, while the euro was at Y110.27 from Y112.01. The U.K. pound was at $1.6320 from $1.6394. The dollar was at CHF0.7548 from CHF0.7675.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 74.852 from about 74.598.\par \par \uc2 While it was U.S. debt that was downgraded on Friday, the dollar retained enough appeal as a relatively stable "safe haven" to attract nervous investors on Monday. Fears of an already fragile U.S. fiscal picture getting worse feeds into existing concern that the U.S. economy could drag down other healthier economies on the globe. With the U.S. debt-ceiling talks and any imminent debt default out of the way, the dollar could again resume its function as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  along with the franc and the yen. Aside from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being backed by the world's largest economy and government debt market, the dollar--recent low-yield and Washington in-fighting aside--has traditionally acted as one of the world's safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on the fact that it is the world's reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the most actively traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "Traders are increasingly taking into account a U.S. recession," said Paresh Upadhyaya, head of Americas G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 Merrill Lynch\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Other safe havens also face the threat of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Switzerland have both recently attempted to halt their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' rise, without much success so far.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, investors ignored the threat of further Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling off the dollar by 1% against the yen. Commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weakened as the price of oil and stocks continued to fall throughout the day. Both the Australian and New Zealand dollars fell nearly 2% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 -By Andrew J. Johnson, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3092; andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com [ 08-08-11 1701ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110808e7880005f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
