\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2011\par 05:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: OBAMA AND S&P VIE FOR CREDIBILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration and ratings firm Standard and Poor's have embarked on a battle for credibility that could shape the ultimate impact of the U.S. debt downgrade as well as their own reputations. (published 0100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: GEITHNER ON NBC: US TREASURYS REMAINS SAFE, S&P SHOWED 'TERRIBLE JUDGEMENT' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner Sunday sharply criticized ratings company Standard & Poors for downgrading U.S. debt, and said U.S. treasurys remains a safe place to invest. (published 0042 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YUAN SOARS TO FRESH HIGH ON PBOC GUIDANCE AFTER US CREDIT DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese yuan surged to a fresh high against the U.S. dollar Monday morning on aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guidance after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgraded the U.S.'s top-notch credit rating. (published 0237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: G-7 PLEDGES COORDINATED STEPS TO CALM FINANCIAL MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven industrial nations pledged Monday to take coordinated steps to ensure financial markets have sufficient liquidity and operate properly, seeking to quell an intensifying global crisis as financial markets are rocked by the euro-zone debt crisis and the loss of the U.S. triple-A credit rating. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF CHIEF: G-7 COMMITMENT TO ENSURE STABILITY, LIQUIDITY WILL HELP CONFIDENCE, SPUR GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Monetary Fund chief Sunday welcomed the commitment by finance ministers from Group of Seven industrialized economies to take all necessary and coordinated action to ensure stability and liquidity in the financial markets. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ECB TO 'ACTIVELY IMPLEMENT' SECURITIES MARKETS PROGRAM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said late Sunday it will "actively implement" its government bond-buying program, leaving the door open for purchasing Italian and Spanish government bonds. (published 2207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P: NO IMMEDIATE IMPACT ON ASIA PACIFIC SOVEREIGN RATINGS FROM US DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services said Monday its recent downgrade of the U.S. sovereign credit rating "in and of itself" will have no impact on the ratings of Asia-Pacific sovereigns. (published 0222 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: 10-YEAR US TREASURY YIELD RISES SLIGHTLY FOLLOWING S&P DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasurys rose only slightly early Monday, despite \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  unprecedented downgrade of its previously perfect rating on U.S. government debt. (published 0245 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ASIAN SHARES FALL, DOLLAR DOWN; US DEBT PAIN RAISES NEW WORRIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were sold off and the U.S. dollar was broadly weaker after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  historic downgrade of U.S. government debt triggered fresh concerns about the outlook for the world's largest economy and global growth. (published 0040 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TELLS G-7 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AIMED AT COUNTERING ONE-SIDED MOVES \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister said Monday he explained to Group of Seven member nations that the nation's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week was aimed at countering one-sided moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market at a time when the economy has struggled to recover from the March 11 earthquake. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ LEAVING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS IN MARKET SO FAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  did not absorb any same-day funds from the short-term money market at its morning \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday, suggesting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is leaving funds generated from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday in the banking system. (published 0033 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOVT EDANO: JAPAN WELCOMES MEASURES TAKEN BY US AND EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Monday that the nation welcomes measures taken by the U.S. and Europe to counteract a global economic slowdown. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS SPOKE TO GEITHNER ON COORDINATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasurer Wayne Swan said Monday he spoke to U.S. Treasury Secretary Timothy Geithner overnight on the topic of the U.S. downgrade by Standard and Poor's and the need for global cooperation among major economies. (published 0022 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA NEWSPAPER WARNS OF FINANCIAL TURMOIL AFTER US RATING DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The downgrade of the U.S. government's credit rating has raised the risk of a fresh round of global financial turmoil, the China Securities Journal said Monday, adding to domestic criticism of the U.S. government's fiscal management. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ECONOMIST: ONGOING CRISIS SHOULD TEACH CHINA TO ENCOURAGE PRIVATE INVESTMENT - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should learn from the ongoing financial crisis and encourage private capital to lead investment, the state-run China Securities Journal said Monday quoting a senior government economist writing on his microblog. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: CHINA SHOULD DIVERSIFY AWAY FROM US TREASURYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The downgrade of U.S. debt by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and the extended battle over the U.S. debt ceiling, carry a "deep lesson" for China that it must further diversify its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  holdings, a Chinese government researcher said in an essay Monday. (published 0151 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA GOVERNMENT RESEARCHER: NO BROAD SELL-OFF OF US TREASURYS AFTER CREDIT CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Chinese government researcher said he doesn't expect a broad sell-off of U.S. Treasurys in the near to medium term despite the first downgrade of the U.S. credit rating by a major ratings agency, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -backed Financial News reported Monday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA JULY NEW YUAN LOANS AROUND CNY550BLN-650BLN-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banks are expected to have issued CNY550 billion-CNY650 billion of new yuan loans last month, the state-run China Securities Journal reported Monday, citing an unnamed source. (published 2313 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN JUNE CURRENT ACCOUNT SURPLUS FALL LARGER THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's current account surplus continued its post-March 11 disaster slide in June, posting a sharper-than-expected fall in June as the output slowdown that practically brought auto production to a standstill stymied exports and overseas investment income continued to rise. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: HKMA: FIXED EXCHANGE RATE HAS SERVED HK WELL; NO NEED TO CHANGE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Norman Chan Monday reiterated that the city is committed to maintaining the local dollar's peg to the U.S. dollar, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  rating agency downgraded U.S. debt late last week. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES BUDGET SECRETARY: TO KEEP 2011 BUDGET DEFICIT GOAL AMID HIGHER SPENDING PLANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines will keep its budget deficit goal for 2011 amid plans to accelerate spending in the second half of the year, Budget Secretary Florencio Abad said Monday. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA DEVELOPMENT BANK, BANK OF COMMUNICATIONS TO ISSUE DIM SUM BONDS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Development Bank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and Bank of Communications Co. are set to be the next to issue yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong, following a CNY20 billion issuance by China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Apple Daily reported Monday. (published 0108 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par WSJ: IN TOKYO, A CALM, EARLY OPENING TO THE TRADING DAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the markets opened Monday morning in Tokyo, the mood was one of extreme concentration, not chaos, in one of Asia's leading financial centers. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par POINT OF VIEW: DESPITE PAST CRITIQUES, S&P ON TARGET ON US \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The irony likely hasn't been lost on either critics or supporters of the major credit-ratings agencies that one of the group's most controversial calls--the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgrade of U.S. long-term debt to AA+ from the long-enjoyed AAA--didn't produce a dime of revenue. (published 2157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: CURSE OF THE TRIPLE-A RATING HAUNTS U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  has fired a warning shot across the U.S. bow. But that could be a blessing if it helps the U.S. start to escape the curse of its former triple-A rating. (published 2132 GMT) [ 08-08-11 0300GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110808e7880007k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
