\par\par \b \uc2 Options suggest more franc gains, yen seen capped\b0\par\par\uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2011\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Swiss vols elevated as traders wary of more spot strength\par \par \uc2 * Risk reversals also heavily skewed for Swiss gains\par \par \uc2 * Yen vols, risk reversals show BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  subdues market\par \par \uc2 By Neal Armstrong\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 8 (Reuters) - Swiss franc options are at extreme levels, showing investors are braced for more gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while yen options pricing suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have capped the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength.\par \par \uc2 Both the yen and the franc have soared in recent weeks as investors chase safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid renewed financial market stress, leading the Japanese and Swiss central banks to take measures last week to counter the gains.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  cut interest rates, the Bank of Japan undertook a huge yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a solo effort to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower and protect the export-driven Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 However, options markets have shown investors less than impressed by the SNB's attempts to curb franc strength and implied volatility -- the market's estimation of future movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- has since gone even higher.\par \par \uc2 This suggests the market is wary of further rapid moves in the franc and the risk of further SNB action.\par \par \uc2 One-month implied euro/Swiss vol trades at record levels of around 20 percent according to IFR, a Thomson Reuters service, edging above previous highs seen in the wake of the 2008 collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Volatility traders in the Swiss franc are still saying if the franc goes higher it will be more volatile," said Simon Smollett, options strategist at \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  CIB.\par \par \uc2 "The prices of dollar/Swiss and euro/Swiss options have not come off at all," he added.\par \par \uc2 Options allow investors the right to buy (call) or sell (put) a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a pre-determined "strike" price either to protect against a sharp move or as a bet on such a move.\par \par \uc2 Risk reversals, a measure of the premium required to hold a put or a call in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , remain heavily skewed in favour of Swiss calls -- bets the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise -- at 3.25 in the one-month 25-delta , not far from record levels hit during the Lehman crisis near 4 vols.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect firm demand for volatility along the curve.\par \par \uc2 "It's hard to be short of Swiss vol right now and even the one-week in the mid-20's looks cheap." said an options trader at a European bank.\par \par \uc2 Market players say any options betting on the euro falling further against the franc, which in principle could slow a further sell-off in euro/Swiss spot, are few and far between as the franc's rapid surge to such extreme levels has not left time for many investors to make such bets.\par \par \uc2 YEN SKEW IMPACTED BY BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 In contrast, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last Thursday -- when it is estimated to have sold around 4.5 trillion yen ($56 billion) -- seems to have made an impact in the options market.\par \par \uc2 Risk-reversals briefly flipped their bias immediately after the BOJ action in the very front end, with the one-week\par \par \uc2 moving to favour dollar calls/yen puts for the first time since the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September 2010, while vols sold off as markets factored out any more rapid yen appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The diverging outlooks for options markets in the franc and the yen reflect market skepticism over policymakers' response to the euro zone debt crisis, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 "Since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September 2010 the options market has been respecting the BOJ's stance and the change in bias in one-week risk-reversals is interesting" Smollett added.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday was reported to have bought Spanish, Italian and peripheral euro zone bonds, but investors remain cautious and that is likely to support the Swiss franc against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The Swiss franc is clearly a Europe story and no amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the SNB can save the periphery," said another options trader. "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  addresses the problem."\par \par \uc2 Market players say yen vols are also relatively subdued because some Japanese exporters have budgeted for the dollar to be around 80 yen this year, a potential restriction on yen weakness.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /OPTIONS   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110808e7880012j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
