\par\par \b \uc2 3rd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely Totals Record Y4.46T-Y4.66T\b0\par\par\uc2 720 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 12:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data show yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely totaled around Y4.46 trillion-Y4.66 trillion, the largest ever\par \par \uc2 -- BOJ refrains from draining \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds from market in Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Sterilization of funds seen as unlikely, given additional funding being promised by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Recasts lead, adds details of estimated size of yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2nd-6th paragraphs and trader's comments in 8th paragraph)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Japanese government's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday likely totaled about Y4.46 trillion-Y4.66 trillion, sharply exceeding the previous record amount, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data released Friday indicated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The figure is derived from the Bank of Japan's estimate for its current account balance related to fiscal factors as of Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ said it expects a surplus of Y4.46 trillion, the data showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Excluding the impact of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is counted as a surplus, the market had expected a shortage of up to Y200 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The resulting gap suggests that the size of the MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was around Y4.46 trillion-Y4.66 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This was bigger than many Tokyo traders' expectations of between Y2 trillion-Y4 trillion and would be the largest on record, exceeding the Y2.62 trillion on April 10, 1998, when it bought yen for dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The figure is also much larger than \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's share of the joint Group of Seven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on March 18, which came to Y693 billion, and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's solo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  On Sept. 15, 2010, when it sold Y2.12 billion yen for dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some market participants are now getting worried that the large spending in one-day \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would make further action by the ministry more difficult.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spent too much," said one dealer at a Japanese bank, adding that "we may hear criticisms from lawmakers on the MOF spending this much in the coming days, and that may put a high barrier for the MOF to re-enter the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the yen earlier this week nearing the post-World War II high against the dollar of Y76.25 marked March 17, the finance ministry decided Thursday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to weaken the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After launching the yen-selling campaign in Tokyo trade, Japanese authorities were also seen in the London market, pushing up the dollar above the Y80 level for the first time since July 12. The dollar stood at Y78.46 as of 1043 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a sign of support to the MOF's efforts, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also refrained from draining \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds from the market Friday, suggesting it isn't at this point sterilizing the previous day's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central banks "sterilize" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when they want to keep the extra funds generated from being added to the overall money supply. To do so, they drain from the market the amount of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and thereby ensure that overall liquidity reflects the desired daily supply and demand in the banking system.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Throughout Friday, the BOJ, as widely expected, didn't offer any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that would drain funds beginning Monday. Funds from Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are slated to settle Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts say not sterilizing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  funds could make the MOF's action even more effective by making financial conditions more accommodative, but the real impact of such action may be limited.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Increases in the BOJ's current account balance may not have much direct easing effects ... because it simply means unused money is sitting in banks' accounts" and not injected into the overall economy, said Masaaki Kanno, chief economist at JPMorgan Securities Japan and a former BOJ official.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, Kanno said leaving ample money in the accounts, along with the very rare coordinated move of the MOF's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the BOJ's monetary easing, could have a psychological impact on market participants.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ eased monetary policy further Thursday by expanding its asset-purchase program to Y15 trillion from Y10 trillion and its six-month fixed-rate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to Y15 trillion from Y10 trillion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Megumi Fujikawa, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2786; megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this article [ 05-08-11 1049GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e785001at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
