\par\par \b \uc2 3rd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Ready To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Market Again After Record-Large Spend\b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 13:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy minister suggests \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  again\par \par \uc2 -- Finance minister says paying close attention to stock market\par \par \uc2 -- BOJ data suggests that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was largest on record at Y4.46-Y4.66 trillion\par \par \uc2 -- Extra funds remaining in the market\par \par \uc2 (Updates market rates, BOJ figures showing size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trader reaction, 6th 9th paragraphs.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By George Nishiyama and Tatsuo Ito \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Concerned about the impact of pessimism spreading throughout global markets, Japanese officials said on Friday they stand ready to wade back into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if action is needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Current account figures from the Bank of Japan suggested that the government had sold an estimated Y4.5 trillion, double the previous one-day total for a yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's too hasty to think Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was a one-off measure," Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano, whose ministry is not in charge of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said at a regular press conference.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asked about Tokyo's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy going forward, Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he would pay particular attention to the stock market following the sharp 4% fall in the Dow Jones industrial average overnight. Tokyo shares fell sharply, with the Nikkei Stock Average closing 3.7% lower at 9299.88.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While there were no signs of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities so far on Friday, traders said their action on Thursday showed their determination to push down the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ figures pointed to total spending worth about Y4.46 trillion-Y4.66 trillion. That would be the largest on record, exceeding the Y2.62 trillion on April 10, 1998, when it bought yen for dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The figure is also much larger than \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's share of the joint Group of Seven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on March 18, which came to Y693 billion, and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's solo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  On Sept. 15, 2010, when it sold Y2.12 billion yen for dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan spent too much," said one dealer at a Japanese bank, adding that "we may hear criticism from lawmakers on the MOF spending this much in the coming days, and that may put a high barrier for the MOF to re-enter the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Money market figures from the BOJ also showed that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had left the extra funds in the market, further increasing its already ample liquidity.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  launched the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drive on Thursday in tandem with credit easing by the Bank of Japan, and the concerted move succeeded in pushing the dollar up by more than Y2.5 at one point. The dollar rose above Y80 overnight but later fell back and at 0124 GMT was at Y78.47.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yosano said the authorities in the U.S., Europe, Japan need to coordinate polices to prevent a spread of pessimism throughout the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We must avoid a situation where fear invites more fear," Yosano said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But there has been little evidence of cooperation, and officials have been far from speaking in one voice.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By George Nishiyama and Tatsuo Ito, Dow Jones Newswires; +81-3-6269-2818; george.nishiyama@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this article\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 05, 2011 07:41 ET (11:41 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110805e785004av\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
