\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  CDS Index Widens On Slowdown Fears, MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Support Short-lived\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 11:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's benchmark index for the cost of insuring against credit defaults widened as concerns over a global economic slowdown hurt risk sentiment and triggered stock selloffs around the world.\par \par \uc2 Although the index tightened Thursday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen and the Bank of Japan decided to expand its asset purchase program, the momentum didn't last long in the face of global economic uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 The iTraxx Japan Series 15 rose to 125.5 basis points Friday, compared with 119 basis points at the beginning of the week, Tokyo credit default swaps traders said.\par \par \uc2 The index fell to as low as 117 basis points Thursday, driven by "speculation that an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is positive for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Akira Nomura, credit analyst at Mizuho Securities. A weaker yen helps Japan's key export sector by making their products more competitive overseas and boosting earnings sent back to Japan.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan's decision to pour another Y10 trillion into the economy was also a Japan credit positive, a Tokyo credit default swap trader said.\par \par \uc2 However, risk-sentiment deteriorated sharply Friday with the Nikkei tumbling 3.7% after U.S. stocks plunged Thursday amid concerns over the slowdown in the U.S. economy while widening trends in Italy and Spain government bond yields continued.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the cost of insuring \uc2 Hitachi Ltd\uc2 . (6501.TO) debt tightened while protection for \uc2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\uc2 . (7011.TO) widened, as news broke that the two Japanese heavyweight conglomerates are considering merging major industrial businesses.\par \par \uc2 Market participants are closely watching the U.S. non-farm payrolls data later in the global day to assess whether the widening trend would continue.\par \par \uc2 Individual CDS trades this week include:\par \par \uc2 Monday: iTraxx 119, 118\par \par \uc2 Sharp Corp\uc2 . (6753.TO) five-year at 74, 73 vs 73 on July 6, three-year at 48, 45\par \par \uc2 Tuesday: iTraxx 118.5, 119\par \par \uc2 Sharp at 74 vs Monday's 73\par \par \uc2 Fujitsu Ltd\uc2 . (6702.TO) at 72 vs 73 on July 19\par \par \uc2 Sumitomo Corp\uc2 . (8053.TO) at 68 vs 73 on July 7\par \par \uc2 Nippon Paper Group Inc. (3893.TO) at 113, unchanged from July 4\par \par \uc2 Daiwa Securities Group Inc\uc2 . (8601.TO) at 183\par \par \uc2 Wednesday: iTraxx 121, 121.5, 121.5, 122, 121.5\par \par \uc2 Japan dollar-denominated sovereign CDS at 89.5 vs 87.5 on July 22\par \par \uc2 Toyota Motor Corp\uc2 . (7203.TO) at 69 vs 72.5 on March 14\par \par \uc2 Mitsui & Co. Ltd\uc2 . (8031.TO) at 66 vs 69 on June 20\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi Corp\uc2 . (8058.TO) at 60 vs 63 on July 13\par \par \uc2 Mazda Motor Corp\uc2 . (7261.TO) at 145\par \par \uc2 Thursday: iTraxx 118, 117\par \par \uc2 A switch deal between Series 15 (118) and Series 14 (102) at 16\par \par \uc2 Hitachi Ltd\uc2 . (6501.TO) at 66, 67 vs 71 on July 8\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd\uc2 . (7011.TO) at 61\par \par \uc2 JFE Steel Corp\uc2 . at 79 vs 80.5 on July 20\par \par \uc2 Mitsubishi Estate Co. Ltd\uc2 . (8802.TO) at 65 vs 52 on March 7\par \par \uc2 Komatsu Ltd\uc2 . (6301.TO) at 56 vs 52 on Jan. 24\par \par \uc2 Friday: iTraxx 126, 125, 125.5\par \par \uc2 Japan dollar-denominated sovereign CDS at 93, 94 vs Wednesday's 89.5\par \par \uc2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\uc2  dollar-denominated subordinated at 210 vs 186 on July 6\par \par \uc2 Hitachi at 72 vs Thursday's 67\par \par \uc2 Kobe Steel Ltd\uc2 . (5406.TO) at 91, 95, 96 vs 90 on July 14\par \par \uc2 Nippon Paper Group\uc2  at 120 vs 113 on Aug. 2\par \par \uc2 Panasonic Corp\uc2 . (6752.TO) at 59 vs 50 on July 13\par \par \uc2 Sony Corp\uc2 . (6758.TO) at 90 vs 85 on July 13\par \par \uc2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2784; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 05, 2011 05:57 ET (09:57 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110805e785003kp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
