\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 12:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPE DEBT INSURANCE COSTS RETREAT FROM OPENING HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The cost of insuring European corporate debt against default retreated from earlier highs Friday, as market participants remained on edge after euro-zone debt crisis concerns and fears of a global slowdown hit financial markets around the world.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK PRODUCER PRICE INFLATION BUOYED BY RECORD CLOTHES PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--U.K. factory gate inflation increased in July at the fastest rate for almost three years due to a record rise in clothing and textile prices, official data showed Friday,\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MERKEL, SARKOZY TO DISCUSS EURO-ZONE SITUATION - SPOKESMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BERLIN (Dow Jones)--German Chancellor Angela Merkel will later Friday talk to French President Nicolas Sarkozy over the telephone, with the "current situation in the euro zone" among the issues to be discussed, a Merkel spokesman said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB COENE: FAILURE TO ACT NOW RISKS EURO LONG-TERM EXISTENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Politicians have to improve their communication with markets and take decisions on strengthening economic governance or risk the existence of the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ECB governing council member Luc Coene said Friday. (published 0722 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB'S STARK OPPOSED FURTHER GOVERNMENT BOND BUYS - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Executive Board member Juergen Stark joined Germany's Bundesbank in opposing plans to reactivate the ECB's bond-buying program, a person familiar with the matter said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO SHARES END NEAR 5-MONTH LOW ON GLOBAL ECONOMIC FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks fell sharply Friday as fears of a global economic downturn gripped the market, sending the Nikkei Stock Average to its worst loss in almost five months, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  among several blue chips falling more than 5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA-PACIFIC OFFICIALS EXPRESS CONCERN ON GLOBAL ECONOMIC OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asia-Pacific policymakers Friday voiced concern about the darkening of the global outlook and declared themselves ready to respond, although for now at least inflation appears likely to trump growth fears as the dominant regional risk.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  READY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT AGAIN, CONCERNED OVER SHARE FALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concerned about the impact of pessimism spreading throughout global markets, Japanese officials said on Friday they stand ready to wade back into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if action is needed. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DOWN AMID FALLING CONSTRUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BERLIN (Dow Jones)--German industrial output fell in June amid a plunge in construction activity, data showed Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF SPAIN: COUNTRY'S ECONOMIC RECOVERY LOST MOMENTUM IN 2Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spain's timid economic recovery lost momentum in the second quarter, according to an estimate Friday from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN ECON MINISTER OPPOSES FURTHER EFSF ENHANCEMENT -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--German Economics Minister Philipp Roesler opposes any further enhancement of the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's temporary bailout fund, as recently suggested by European Commission President Jose Manuel Barroso.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU'S REHN: COMMISSION TO PUBLISH REPORT ON EURO BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The European Commission will publish in the autumn a report on the feasibility of individual countries issuing bonds backed by the whole euro zone, European Commissioner for Economic and Monetary Affairs Olli Rehn said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S&P KEEPS IRELAND RATING AT BBB+ WITH STABLE OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Standard and Poor's Corp. Friday maintained its current stance on Ireland's creditworthiness, citing support from the country's open economy and political commitment to stabilize public finances.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALY 2Q GDP RISES 0.3% AS EXPECTED, ANNUAL PACE SLOWS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ROME (Dow Jones)--Italy's economy accelerated as expected in the second quarter, expanding by 0.3% from the first three months of the year, national statistics institute Istat said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION FALLS SHARPLY IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spanish industrial production fell sharply in June in a new sign that growth in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy is slowing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY'S GOVERNMENT NOT WORKING ON POLICY TIGHTENING -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ISTANBUL (Dow Jones)--Turkey's government isn't working on a tightening of its monetary policy, a minister said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NO BOJ DRAINING SUGGESTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS BEING LEFT IN MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as largely expected by market players, refrained from draining funds from the market at its Friday morning money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting that it is not at this point sterilizing the yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the government on the previous day. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNB READY TO TAKE ACTION ON FRANC, SAYS HILDEBRAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take all conceivable and effective measures to stall the Swiss franc's appreciation, if it becomes necessary, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philipp Hildebrand\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in an interview with Swiss daily Neue Zuercher Zeitung published Friday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS JULY CPI DOWN 0.8% ON MONTH; UP 0.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The Swiss consumer price index fell 0.8% on the month in July, driven by lower clothing and energy costs, data released Friday showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA SHARES END DOWN 3.7%, BIGGEST SINGLE-DAY DROP SINCE NOV 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--South Korean shares slumped Friday in their biggest single-day percentage drop in nearly two years, as regional stock markets tumbled amid fears that the global economic recovery is faltering.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA WARNS OF WORSENING GLOBAL OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned Friday of increasing downside risks to the global economic outlook as financial markets rushed to price in aggressive interest rate cuts before the end of the year and the government was moved to reassure markets it has the fire power to fight another international downturn. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: WILL CONTINUE TO WATCH MARKETS CAREFULLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday he will continue to watch financial markets carefully, adding that the fall in Tokyo share prices during the day was largely a result of overnight falls in U.S. share prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SLIGHTLY UPGRADES ECON ASSESSMENT IN AUG FROM PREVIOUS MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan on Friday slightly upgraded its assessment of the economy in August from the previous month, as the economy continues to recover from the devastation of the March 11 earthquake. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF EXPECTED TO APPOINT NEW HEAD OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DIVISION - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Ministry is expected to move ahead with its plan to replace the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market division chief in the coming days, even though the country just began a round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to several people familiar with the matter. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH'S COLQUHOUN: JAPAN'S POLICY FLEXIBILITY IS A SUPPORT 'AT THE MARGIN' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's policy flexibility, as demonstrated by its latest easing measures and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is a support for the sovereign "at the margin," a senior analyst at Fitch Ratings told to Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FOREIGN MINISTER URGES COOPERATION TO BOOST GLOBAL ECONOMIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Foreign Minister Yang Jiechi urged all countries to cooperate to boost the global economy's recovery and to reform the international financial system, as he warned of continuing sovereign debt risks in the U.S. and E.U. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORMER PBOC ADVISER SAYS CHINA MUST FLOAT YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued in a commentary piece on Thursday that the country must float the yuan in order to stop accumulating foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA BANK REGULATOR CALLS ON BANKS TO AID PUBLIC HOUSING PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator on Friday urged banks to extend credit and offer preferential lending rates to support the construction of public housing, in a bid to ease funding shortfalls that have hampered the key government project. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD TO TEST 1.40 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: More weakness to the July 18 higher low at 1.4014 is the main threat, as the decline off 1.4537 has been upgraded. A break below Friday's Asian session low at 1.4055 is expected, and increasing EUR bear momentum would have scope for 1.3981 and 1.3940. Projected resistance lies at 1.4287, but corrective gains appear limited to 1.4203. (published 0718 GMT) [ 05-08-11 1004GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e7850018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
