\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ: Euro Pares Losses In Asia Ahead Of Key US Jobs Report\b0\par\par\uc2 By Geoffrey Rogow in Sydney and George Nishiyama and Tatsuo Ito in Tokyo   \par \uc2 Of THE WALL STREET JOURNAL   \par \uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 11:33\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The euro recovered partly from an earlier plunge by Friday afternoon in Asia, while the yen recovered roughly half what it lost the previous day, but an overnight selloff in riskier assets in New York and London had investors still on edge ahead of Friday's key nonfarm payrolls report in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Early Friday in London, the euro was at $1.4159, up from an earlier low of $1.4055 and from $1.4100 in New York. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was around Y111.08 from Y111.27.\par \par \uc2 Late Friday in Tokyo, the dollar was at Y78.59 after rising above Y80 overnight. The yen notched a sudden, brief dip to an intraday low of Y79.42 against the dollar around midday, according to EBS. Traders in Tokyo said the move was likely due to large trades being executed, and wasn't likely to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A Japanese government official, asked about the move, declined to comment Friday on whether the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 After selling broadly late in New York and early in Asia, the euro recovered some of its lost footing against both the dollar and the Swiss franc. After the Dow Jones Industrial Average lost more than 500 points Thursday, the euro had earlier pushed to a fresh all-time low against the Swiss franc and its lowest point against the dollar since July 18.\par \par \uc2 Partly helping the rebound was a retracement for stocks in Hong Kong and Japan, with those markets coming off their session lows. Traders said flows were subdued ahead of Friday's U.S. nonfarm payrolls report.\par \par \uc2 "It's not about fundamentals right now, it's about preservation of capital with concerns about liquidity in general," said Sue Trinh, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The subdued action came in stark contrast to New York on Thursday, which had one of the busiest sessions of all time for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, according to EBS. Data from EBS in New York showed that trading totaled $405 billion, the third busiest day ever, while activity in the dollar against the yen of $105 billion was an all-time high. There were 252,746 total deals, the second highest ever.\par \par \uc2 Setting the focus of Asian traders on the euro was a decision by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restart buying of troubled euro-zone bonds, which did little to soothe investors or the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The lack of coordination with the efforts there is just killing sentiment about the region," said Robert Rennie, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Japanese officials, concerned about the impact of pessimism spreading throughout global markets, said Friday that they stand ready to wade back into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if action is needed.\par \par \uc2 "It's too hasty to think Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a one-off measure," Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano, whose ministry is not in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said at a regular press conference.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda also said separately he will pay particular attention to the stock market following an overnight fall in the Dow Jones Industrial Average, when asked about Tokyo's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy going forward.\par \par \uc2 "In addition to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, given the Dow's fall, I would like to closely watch the stock market today," Mr. Noda said, adding that Tokyo will take timely and appropriate measures.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the finance ministry appeared to have sold around Y2 trillion to Y4 trillion via Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making it the nation's largest-ever yen-selling in a single day, surpassing the previous record of Y2.125 trillion marked last September.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive on Thursday in tandem with credit easing by the Bank of Japan, and the concerted move succeeded in pushing the dollar up by more than Y2.50 at one point, but Wall Street's sharp fall overnight and renewed concerns about the European economy put upward pressure on the yen.\par \par \uc2 Japan Economy Minister Yosano said the authorities in the U.S., Europe and Japan need to coordinate polices to prevent a spread of pessimism throughout the global economy.\par \par \uc2 "We must avoid a situation where fear invites more fear," Yosano said, adding that he was confident that the governments and central banks of the U.S. and Europe will take sufficient policy steps to avert such a situation.\par \par \uc2 But there has been little evidence of cooperation, and officials have been far from speaking in one voice.\par \par \uc2 Following Japan's action Thursday, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  must be conducted on a multilateral basis, while a U.S. official said Washington didn't back Japan's decision.\par \par \uc2 Asked about their remarks, Mr. Noda declined to comment, adding only that he had been in touch with his overseas counterparts.\par \par \uc2 -By Geoffrey Rogow in Sydney and George Nishiyama and Tatsuo Ito in Tokyo, The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 --Takashi Mochizuki contributed to this article [ 05-08-11 0933GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e7850016l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
