\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan index on economic outlook rises at record\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Leading, coincident indicator indexes both rise in June\par \par \uc2  * BOJ revises up view on economy in August report\par \par \uc2  * Govt, BOJ warn of risks to economic outlook \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, BOJ monthly report)\par \par \uc2  By Kaori Kaneko and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 5 (Reuters) - An index gauging the outlook for Japan's economy rose in June at a record pace from May in a sign that the recovery from the March earthquake is broadening, although the government warned of risks to the outlook such as slowing global growth.\par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan raised its assessment of the economy in its monthly report for August but also warned of potential damage from recent yen rises and heightening uncertainty over the global economy.\par \par \uc2  "Japan's economy is picking up steadily as supply constraints from the quake ease," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the report issued on Friday, adding that a return to a moderate recovery was projected as factory output rebounds.\par \par \uc2  "But both advanced and emerging economies are facing high uncertainties. The yen is strengthening so the move's impact on exports need to be monitored carefully," it said.\par \par \uc2  Japan's index of leading indicators, a gauge of the economy a few months ahead that is compiled from data such as the number of job offers and consumer sentiment, rose 3.8 points from May, the biggest increase on record, the government said on Friday.\par \par \uc2  Production of automobiles and electronic goods improved and inventories of electronic goods fell sharply, while business and consumer sentiment picked up, driving the improvement in the index, it said.\par \par \uc2  The index of coincident indicators, comprising data measuring the current state of the economy, rose a preliminary 2.5 points. The government revised up its assessment of the index, saying that it suggested an improvement in the economy.\par \par \uc2  "Along with an improvement in production, such as for autos, from declines in March and April, employment and consumption have also recovered," Minoru Masujima, director of the department of business statistics at the Cabinet Office, told a briefing.\par \par \uc2  "The biggest risk is how the economies of the United States and Europe will affect Japan, and whether China will further tighten policy to prevent economic overheating."\par \par \uc2  The government and the BOJ have become increasingly confident that Japan's economy will resume a moderate recovery in autumn as it shakes off supply constraints due to the March earthquake.\par \par \uc2  But that view has fallen into doubt as the yen's surge and the global economic slowdown cloud the outlook for the export reliant economy, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to ease monetary policy. \par \par \uc2 (Editing by Edmund Klamann)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/COINCIDENT  (UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110805e785000fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
