\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ITALIAN, SPANISH BOND YIELD SPREADS VS BUNDS AT EURO-ERA HIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Italian 10-year bond yields hit fresh euro-era highs early Friday as fears that the euro-zone debt crisis is spiraling out of control gripped financial markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO SHARES END NEAR 5-MONTH LOW ON GLOBAL ECONOMIC FEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks fell sharply Friday as fears of a global economic downturn gripped the market, sending the Nikkei Stock Average to its worst loss in almost five months, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sony\f28 \uc2 \f2  among several blue chips falling more than 5%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASIA-PACIFIC OFFICIALS EXPRESS CONCERN ON GLOBAL ECONOMIC OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Asia-Pacific policymakers Friday voiced concern about the darkening of the global outlook and declared themselves ready to respond, although for now at least inflation appears likely to trump growth fears as the dominant regional risk.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  READY TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MKT AGAIN, CONCERNED OVER SHARE FALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concerned about the impact of pessimism spreading throughout global markets, Japanese officials said on Friday they stand ready to wade back into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets if action is needed. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NO BOJ DRAINING SUGGESTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS BEING LEFT IN MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as largely expected by market players, refrained from draining funds from the market at its Friday morning money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , suggesting that it is not at this point sterilizing the yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the government on the previous day. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MERKEL, SARKOZY TO DISCUSS EURO-ZONE SITUATION - SPOKESMAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BERLIN (Dow Jones)--German Chancellor Angela Merkel will later Friday talk to French President Nicolas Sarkozy over the telephone, with the "current situation in the euro zone" among the issues to be discussed, a Merkel spokesman said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ECB COENE: FAILURE TO ACT NOW RISKS EURO LONG-TERM EXISTENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Politicians have to improve their communication with markets and take decisions on strengthening economic governance or risk the existence of the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ECB governing council member Luc Coene said Friday. (published 0722 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN ECON MINISTER OPPOSES FURTHER EFSF ENHANCEMENT -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRANKFURT (Dow Jones)--German Economics Minister Philipp Roesler opposes any further enhancement of the European Financial Stability Facility, the euro zone's temporary bailout fund, as recently suggested by European Commission President Jose Manuel Barroso.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU'S REHN: COMMISSION TO PUBLISH REPORT ON EURO BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The European Commission will publish in the autumn a report on the feasibility of individual countries issuing bonds backed by the whole euro zone, European Commissioner for Economic and Monetary Affairs Olli Rehn said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION FALLS SHARPLY IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MADRID (Dow Jones)--Spanish industrial production fell sharply in June in a new sign that growth in the euro zone's fourth-largest economy is slowing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNB READY TO TAKE ACTION ON FRANC, SAYS HILDEBRAND - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to take all conceivable and effective measures to stall the Swiss franc's appreciation, if it becomes necessary, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philipp Hildebrand\f28 \uc2 \f2  says in an interview with Swiss daily Neue Zuercher Zeitung published Friday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWISS JULY CPI DOWN 0.8% ON MONTH; UP 0.5% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The Swiss consumer price index fell 0.8% on the month in July, driven by lower clothing and energy costs, data released Friday showed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA SHARES END DOWN 3.7%, BIGGEST SINGLE-DAY DROP SINCE NOV 2009 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--South Korean shares slumped Friday in their biggest single-day percentage drop in nearly two years, as regional stock markets tumbled amid fears that the global economic recovery is faltering.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S RBA WARNS OF WORSENING GLOBAL OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warned Friday of increasing downside risks to the global economic outlook as financial markets rushed to price in aggressive interest rate cuts before the end of the year and the government was moved to reassure markets it has the fire power to fight another international downturn. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FIN MIN NODA: WILL CONTINUE TO WATCH MARKETS CAREFULLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday he will continue to watch financial markets carefully, adding that the fall in Tokyo share prices during the day was largely a result of overnight falls in U.S. share prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SLIGHTLY UPGRADES ECON ASSESSMENT IN AUG FROM PREVIOUS MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan on Friday slightly upgraded its assessment of the economy in August from the previous month, as the economy continues to recover from the devastation of the March 11 earthquake. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN MOF EXPECTED TO APPOINT NEW HEAD OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DIVISION - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Finance Ministry is expected to move ahead with its plan to replace the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market division chief in the coming days, even though the country just began a round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to several people familiar with the matter. (published 0559 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH'S COLQUHOUN: JAPAN'S POLICY FLEXIBILITY IS A SUPPORT 'AT THE MARGIN' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's policy flexibility, as demonstrated by its latest easing measures and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is a support for the sovereign "at the margin," a senior analyst at Fitch Ratings told to Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FOREIGN MINISTER URGES COOPERATION TO BOOST GLOBAL ECONOMIC RECOVERY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Foreign Minister Yang Jiechi urged all countries to cooperate to boost the global economy's recovery and to reform the international financial system, as he warned of continuing sovereign debt risks in the U.S. and E.U. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FORMER PBOC ADVISER SAYS CHINA MUST FLOAT YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued in a commentary piece on Thursday that the country must float the yuan in order to stop accumulating foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA BANK REGULATOR CALLS ON BANKS TO AID PUBLIC HOUSING PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator on Friday urged banks to extend credit and offer preferential lending rates to support the construction of public housing, in a bid to ease funding shortfalls that have hampered the key government project. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: FRENCH TRADE DEFICIT NARROWS TO EUR5.6B IN JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's trade deficit narrowed in June and May's figure was revised lower, data from the national customs office showed Friday. (published 0747 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SETS FRAMEWORK FOR MUNICIPAL BONDS TRIAL - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has set a framework for a pilot program under which local governments can directly issue bonds to repay some of the borrowings by their financing vehicles, the state-owned Shanghai Securities News reported Friday, citing an unnamed source. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA MINISTER: ALL PRECAUTIONS BEING TAKEN TO KEEP BAD LOANS IN CHECK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian state-run banks are taking all precautions to keep a check on bad loans, which have been rising in the past couple of years, a federal junior finance minister said Friday. (published 0743 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IMF: SOUTH KOREAN ECONOMIC OUTLOOK REMAINS 'FAVORABLE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic outlook remains "favorable," with growth expected to remain robust, allowing policy makers to begin tightening monetary policy, the International Monetary Fund said Thursday in a report. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA AUTHORITIES TO STEP UP MONITORING OF MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean authorities said Friday they would step up the monitoring of financial markets amid heightened volatility stemming from concerns about the economies of the U.S. and Europe. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA TREASURER SWAN: COUNTRY HAS CAPACITY TO ACT IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Deputy Prime Minister and Treasurer Wayne Swan said on Friday the country's robust fiscal position gives the government the necessary cushion to stoke growth if required. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: EUR/USD TO TEST 1.40 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: More weakness to the July 18 higher low at 1.4014 is the main threat, as the decline off 1.4537 has been upgraded. A break below Friday's Asian session low at 1.4055 is expected, and increasing EUR bear momentum would have scope for 1.3981 and 1.3940. Projected resistance lies at 1.4287, but corrective gains appear limited to 1.4203. (published 0718 GMT) [ 05-08-11 0801GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e7850010x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
