uggesting that it is not at this point sterilizing the yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the government on the previous day. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par RBA CUTS 2011 GROWTH OUTLOOK BUT REBOUND LIKELY SWIFT; INFLATION TROUBLING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday revised sharply lower its forecast for economic growth in 2011, but said it continues to expect a full-blooded recovery in 2012, while inflation is set to remain a nagging problem for some years. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FITCH'S COLQUHOUN: JAPAN'S POLICY FLEXIBILITY IS A SUPPORT 'AT THE MARGIN' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's policy flexibility, as demonstrated by its latest easing measures and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is a support for the sovereign "at the margin," a senior analyst at Fitch Ratings told to Dow Jones Newswires Friday. (published 0124 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: CHINA'S 2011 INFLATION MAY TOP 5% - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation rate may climb above 5% this year, although the pace of price rises may ease slightly in the second half of the year, a state researcher said in a newspaper commentary Friday. (published 0153 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FORMER PBOC ADVISER SAYS CHINA MUST FLOAT YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A former adviser to China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  argued in a commentary piece on Thursday that the country must float the yuan in order to stop accumulating foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULDN'T CHANGE MONETARY POLICY DESPITE COMPLAINTS - PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shouldn't make a big change to its monetary policy despite "some voices" calling for a loosening, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -backed paper argued in an editorial Friday. (published 0043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: SHOULD STOP RAISING BANKS' RESERVE REQUIREMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China should stop raising the reserve requirement for banks, and consider lowering the requirement for small- and medium-sized banks when inflation falls back to below 4%, a researcher with a government think-tank wrote in an commentary in the Economic Information Daily Friday. (published 0152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA BANK REGULATOR CALLS ON BANKS TO AID PUBLIC HOUSING PLAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banking regulator on Friday urged banks to extend credit and offer preferential lending rates to support the construction of public housing, in a bid to ease funding shortfalls that have hampered the key government project. (published 0356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SETS FRAMEWORK FOR MUNICIPAL BONDS TRIAL - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has set a framework for a pilot program under which local governments can directly issue bonds to repay some of the borrowings by their financing vehicles, the state-owned Shanghai Securities News reported Friday, citing an unnamed source. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: SOUTH KOREAN ECONOMIC OUTLOOK REMAINS 'FAVORABLE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic outlook remains "favorable," with growth expected to remain robust, allowing policy makers to begin tightening monetary policy, the International Monetary Fund said Thursday in a report. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA AUTHORITIES TO STEP UP MONITORING OF MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean authorities said Friday they would step up the monitoring of financial markets amid heightened volatility stemming from concerns about the economies of the U.S. and Europe. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA TREASURER SWAN: COUNTRY HAS CAPACITY TO ACT IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Deputy Prime Minister and Treasurer Wayne Swan said on Friday the country's robust fiscal position gives the government the necessary cushion to stoke growth if required. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: INDONESIA 2Q GDP UP 6.49% ON YEAR; UP 2.9% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's economy grew 6.49% in the second quarter from a year earlier, accelerating slightly from 6.47% in the first quarter, driven mainly by rising investment and exports, the official Central Statistics Agency said Friday. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINE JULY INFLATION 4.6% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inflation in the Philippines stood at 4.6% in July, supported by food, fuel and clothing prices as well as utility rates, data released by the National Statistics Office Friday showed. (published 0121 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: CHINA CONSUMER INFLATION LIKELY REMAINED HIGH IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's consumer inflation likely remained high in July, though slightly lower than in the previous month thanks to moderating prices of some key food items such as pork, a survey of economists showed Friday. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WSJ: CAPITALS ON GUARD AGAINST RISING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 No country seems to want a rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --and that poses a problem for a world economy struggling with weakening prospects for growth in the world's biggest developed nations. (published 2344 GMT) [ 05-08-11 0401GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e785000a2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
