\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2011\par 03:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN JULY FOREIGN RESERVES AT RECORD HIGH - MOF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's foreign reserves rose Y13.07 billion on month to a record high at Y1.151 trillion in July, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0059 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOT AIMED AT CERTAIN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LEVEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday that Japanese authorities were not aiming for a certain level of exchange rates in their market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's strength. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ECONOMY MINISTER: PREMATURE TO ASSUME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IS ONE-TIME DEAL \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy minister said Friday it is premature to assume Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was one-time measure, and said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be conducted with appropriate timing. (published 0021 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NO BOJ DRAINING OP, SUGGESTING SOME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS BEING LEFT IN MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  refrained from draining funds at its Friday morning money market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in a sign that it is not at this point sterilizing the yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the government on the previous day. (published 0034 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF SOLD Y2T-Y4T IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THURS - TRADERS \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold around Y2 trillion to Y4 trillion via Thursday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said Friday, making it the nation's largest-ever yen-selling in a single day. (published 0047 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO FACES HEAVY SELLING PRESSURE IN EARLY ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro faced the brunt of Asian traders' selling early Friday as a sell-off in riskier assets in New York and London had investors readjusting their portfolios. (published 2353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF: SOUTH KOREAN ECONOMIC OUTLOOK REMAINS 'FAVORABLE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's economic outlook remains "favorable," with growth expected to remain robust, allowing policy makers to begin tightening monetary policy, the International Monetary Fund said Thursday in a report. (published 0003 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SWAN SAYS ECONOMIC FUNDAMENTALS REMAIN STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Deputy Prime Minister and Treasurer Wayne Swan said Friday while the country isn't immune to the dislocation sweeping through global markets, the underlying economy remains strong with growth in the Asia region. (published 2338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA JULY PERFORMANCE OF CONSTRUCTION INDEX +0.3 PTS TO 36.1 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's construction sector continued to contract in July for the 14th consecutive month, dragged by weak home building, a performance gauge produced by an industry group published Friday shows. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA SHOULDN'T CHANGE MONETARY POLICY DESPITE COMPLAINTS - PAPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shouldn't make a big change to its monetary policy despite "some voices" calling for a loosening, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -backed paper argued in an editorial Friday. (published 0043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA RESEARCHER: CHINA ECONOMY NEEDS TO SLOW SLIGHTLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's economy needs to slow slightly and stabilize, a researcher with a government think-tank wrote in a commentary in the China Securities Journal Friday. (published 0019 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par WSJ: CAPITALS ON GUARD AGAINST RISING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 No country seems to want a rising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --and that poses a problem for a world economy struggling with weakening prospects for growth in the world's biggest developed nations. (published 2344 GMT) [ 05-08-11 0101GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110805e7850002q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
