\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: BOJ Easing,  \highlight22\uc2 Japan FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Are 'Positive Actions'\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 11:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 05:44 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: Japan's 'Big Credit Challenges Remain'\par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 05:45 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2 : Japan's Challenges Are Fiscal Consolidation, Economic Revitalization\par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 05:46 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: Effect Of BOJ, MOF Actions Probably Limited Over Time\par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 05:46 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: BOJ Easing To Help Offset Deflationary Pressures, Aid Recovery\par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 05:47 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Lead Sovereign Analyst For Japan \uc2 Tom Byrne\uc2  Spoke To Dow Jones\par \par \uc2 4 Aug 2011 06:12 EDT DJ  \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: Japan Action 'Positive'; Big Credit Challenges Remain\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Natasha Brereton-Fukui \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--New easing measures by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen are "positive actions," but their impact is likely to be limited over time and they don't remove the "big credit challenges" the country faces, a senior analyst at Moody's Investors Service said Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan stepped into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Thursday, launching a yen-selling campaign that was backed up by Y10 trillion in easing measures from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as officials said they needed to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  lead sovereign analyst for Japan \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Byrne\f28 \uc2 \f2  told Dow Jones Newswires that the BOJ's easing would help to offset deflationary pressures and to some extent aid the recovery of economic activity from various constraints caused by March's devastating earthquake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He noted that the yen's climb was becoming the No. 1 concern for exporters, now that the quake-damaged supply chain is normalizing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "BOJ easing and MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are positive actions, although they will probably have limited effects over time," Byrne said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "However, Japan's big credit challenges remain--fiscal consolidation and economic growth revitalization."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  is nearing the end of a three-month assessment period on Japan's Aa2 sovereign rating, having put it on review for possible downgrade May 31.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Natasha Brereton-Fukui, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4044; natasha.brereton-fukui@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 04, 2011 06:12 ET (10:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020110804e784002mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
