\par\par \b \uc2 RUBBER-Tokyo futures ease on global econ worries\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 10:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Key Tokyo rubber futures eased on Thursday on concerns over the global economic outlook, erasing gains made earlier on the yen's drop after authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The key Tokyo Commodity Exchange rubber contract for January delivery <0#2JRU:> inched down 0.6 yen to settle at 390.5 yen per kg.\par \par \uc2 The most active Shanghai rubber contract for January delivery closed nearly flat at 35,680 yuan ($5,545.453)per tonne on Thursday, compared to the previous close of 35,685 yuan. Volume picked up to 503,444 lots from Wednesday's 452,264 lots.\par \par \uc2 Traders said concerns about global growth and a sluggish Shanghai market weighed on sentiment, helping to wipe out gains made on a weakening yen. A weaker yen inflates the value of yen-priced TOCOM rubber futures.\par \par \uc2 Japan sold the yen in the market and its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased monetary policy on Thursday, following Switzerland in efforts to tame \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoyed by safe-haven demand from investors fretting about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei stock average came off five-week lows on Thursday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary easing, but gave up earlier gains as worries about the health of the global economy dominated.\par \par \uc2 Weak U.S. data raised concerns the key U.S. jobs data for July due on Friday could also be disappointing.\par \par \uc2 The pace of growth in the U.S. services sector ticked down unexpectedly in July to the lowest level since February 2010 and the number of jobs created by the private sector also slowed, reports showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Two key factors need to be watched with regard to the outlook for TOCOM rubber futures, said Daryl Guppy, chief executive officer of Guppytraders.com.\par \par \uc2 "The factors I watch are oil price behaviour -- look for breakout above $100 -- and weakness in the US and euro economies which cannot be offset by increase in China demand," said Guppy, referring to the world's largest rubber consumer.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude dropped to a four-week low on Thursday, erasing early gains after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with investors steering clear of riskier assets such as commodities.\par \par \uc2 For morning and afternoon prices at Thailand's state-run central rubber market, click on <RUB-BKK3>.\par \par \uc2 For other physical rubber prices in Thailand, click on<RUB-BKK1> <RUB-BKK2>.\par \par \uc2 For more details on Indonesian and Malaysian prices click on and .\par \par \uc2 * Reuters Terminal users can see cash and futures rubber prices by double clicking on the codes in the brackets:\par \par \uc2 - Tokyo rubber futures -- <0#JRU:>\par \par \uc2 - Central Japan rubber futures -- <0#JRI:><0#JOS:>\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Shanghai rubber futures     -- <0#SNR:>\par - Singapore rubber futures    -- <0#SRS:><0#SRU:>\par                                <0#STF:>\par - Thai rubber futures            <0#ARU:><0#ASR20:>\par - All rubber news             \par - Tokyo rubber report         \par - Shanghai rubber report      \par - Thailand rubber report      \par - Asian rubber report         \par - Indonesian rubber report    \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For Related News and other topics, double click on one of these codes: SPEED GUIDES ($1 = 6.434 Chinese Yuan)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Chikako Mogi in Tokyo and Lewa Pardomuan in Singapore; Editing by Joseph Radford)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-RUBBER   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110804e784000oi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
