\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 6-Japan acts to tame yen, follows Swiss move on franc\b0\par\par\uc2 1,250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 10:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finance minister confirms solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocks yen from 77.10 to 80.20\par \par \uc2 * Traders say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far is 1 trln yen ($12.5 bln\par \par \uc2 * BOJ boosts asset buying to amplify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effect\par \par \uc2 * U.S. official says U.S. did not support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds U.S. official, Trichet comments, updates markets)\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Japan sold one trillion yen ($12.5 billion) and loosened its monetary reins on Thursday, joining Switzerland in efforts to tame \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  buoyed by safe-haven demand from investors fretting about the deteriorating health of the global economy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it continued in London trading hours, pushed the yen <JPY=> to a three-week low of 80.20 per dollar from around 77.10, a more extensive yen move compared with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March this year and September 2010.\par \par \uc2 U.S. traders said Tokyo seemed to have backed away from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the North American market session, allowing the yen to recover to 79.120 <JPY=EBS>, a 2.7 percent rise against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Japan's action followed days of official warnings that the yen had risen so much that it threatened to derail its recovery from the destruction wrought by the March 11 magnitude 9.0 earthquake, a deadly tsunami and an ensuing nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had consulted its international partners, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own to stem what it considered speculative and disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 The United States did not support the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a U.S. official said, declining to elaborate on whether that meant Washington disapproved of the action.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Jean-Claude Trichet added that Japan's move was not part of a multilateral process, unlike a March \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  done jointly by the Group of Seven economies.\par \par \uc2 "We consider that such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have to be made on the basis of a multilateral consensus," Trichet told a news conference in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 Hours later after the Finance Ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined the fray, boosting funds for buying financial assets to 15 trillion yen from 10 trillion yen, under a scheme established in October 2010 to shore up market confidence and support the economy.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to be working in sync with the finance ministry, and that is different from past times when they eased policy," said Koichi Ono, senior strategist at Daiwa Securities Capital Markets. "It's a message that they are willing to act to stop the yen from appreciating further."\par \par \uc2 Analysts doubted though that even a combination of yen selling and monetary easing could stem a global shift away from the dollar and other riskier assets if Tokyo were to continue acting on its own.\par \par \uc2 "The yen's advance reflects the difficult economic and fiscal situation of both the U.S. and the euro zone, so even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, it won't be able to combat the yen's rise in the long run on its own," said Takashi Kamiya, chief economist at T&D Asset Management Co.\par \par \uc2 <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 -easing combo work? \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                       [ID:L3E7J40A5]\par  Policymakers on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action, easing         \par                                      [ID:nL3E7J41GF]\par  GRAPHIC on yen,\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 :\par                       \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyf82s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyf82s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  Citi sees more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/gum92s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/gum92s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  World interest rates:      \par                       \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xuc92s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xuc92s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  G7 in rare \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action after yen surge      \par                                      [ID:nL3E7EH3HN]\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken yen in September\par                                      [ID:nTOE68E02W]\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indeed, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Economy Minister Kaoru Yosano pressed on Thursday for Group of Seven and Group of 20 officials to discuss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a global issue. [ID:nL3E7J41Z3]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The coordinated action with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was important for Prime Minister Naoto Kan and his government, beset by poor ratings and struggling with the aftermath of Japan's worst disaster in generations and the world's gravest nuclear crisis since Chernobyl 25 years ago.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Japan is just in the process of recovering from a natural disaster, so these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves are certain to have a negative impact on the economy and financial markets," Noda told reporters in justifying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SWISS TRIGGER\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had sold more than one trillion yen in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far on Thursday, a day after the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised markets by cutting interest rates to try to weaken the Swiss franc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors have seen the Swiss franc and the yen as a safer refuge among G10 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from a deepening euro debt crisis and speculation that the U.S. economy could be slipping into recession and could lose its coveted AAA credit rating.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the Swiss rate cut may have influenced the timing of Japan's move, which surprised some traders because the yen had backed off levels close to a record high of 76.25 per dollar, which was hit shortly after the March quake.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Yesterday's monetary easing by Switzerland provided the push because if Japan didn't respond this would push the yen still higher," said Nagayuki Yamagishi, a strategist at Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The moves by Switzerland and Japan could now put pressure on the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which reviews policy on Thursday, to resume bond buying or other measures, since the euro zone crisis is a major factor behind the rise in the franc and yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Other bold policy manoeuvres could be in the pipeline," said Gareth Berry, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 'NEVER SAY NEVER'\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan cut short its scheduled two-day meeting that started on Thursday to announce the easing of policy. It left its benchmark rate steady at 0-0.1 percent. [ID:nL3E7J405R]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With rates pegged near zero, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been using the size of the asset buying pool as the main gauge of its policy stance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The release of extra funds in addition to cash spent on foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen as a way of making the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more effective by boosting yen supply.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asked whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would do more, Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We think we took enough steps after carefully examining economic and price developments as well as the risks to the outlook. Having said that, the economy is a living thing. We central bankers tend to say: 'Never say never.'"\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Until recently the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sounded confident that it had done enough to support the economy and that Japan would exit recession later this year with the help of reconstruction spending following the March disaster and a recovery in exports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the yen's nearly 5 percent climb over the past month cast doubt on such a scenario and both the government and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been under growing pressure from Japanese exporters, including \f28 \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  , to tame the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen selling gave a lift to export shares in Tokyo trading and lifted the Nikkei average <.N225> off five-week lows. [ID:nL3E7J41T2]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Noda would not give away any details of Thursday's action, but traders said authorities continued sporadic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , including in London. Some said it could eventually add up to a similar amount as 2.1 trillion Tokyo sold in its last solo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in September 2010.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=79.90 yen)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Rie Ishiguro and Kaori Kaneko in Tokyo and David Lawder in Washington; Writing by Tomasz Janowski; Editing by Neil Fullick and Kenneth Barry)\f28 \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN  (WRAPUP 6, PIX, TV)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110804e7840001a\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rs